1
00:01:02,530 --> 00:01:04,950
Hunger strike? How long has this been going on?

2
00:01:04,950 --> 00:01:06,840
She hasn't had a thing yesterday or today.

3
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:08,840
-Sending meals up to her regularly?  -Yes, sir.

4
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:11,130
Why don't you jam it down her throat?

5
00:01:11,130 --> 00:01:13,580
lt's not that simple, Mr. Andrews.

6
00:01:13,580 --> 00:01:17,400
l'll talk to her myself. Have some food brought up to her.

7
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:19,120
Yes, sir.

8
00:01:20,180 --> 00:01:22,620
l won't eat a thing until you let me off this boat.

9
00:01:22,710 --> 00:01:25,390
Come now, Ellie. You know l'll have my way.

10
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:28,690
Not this time, you won't! l'm already married to him.

11
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:31,630
You'll never live under the same roof with him. l'll see to it.

12
00:01:31,860 --> 00:01:35,570
Can't you get it through your head, King Westley and l are married!

13
00:01:35,570 --> 00:01:39,140
Definitely, legally, actually married! lt's over, it's finished.

14
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:41,360
There's not a thing you can do about it. l'm over 21 and so is he.

15
00:01:41,430 --> 00:01:43,770
Would you be interested that while you've been onboard...

16
00:01:43,870 --> 00:01:45,650
...l've arranged to have your marriage annulled.

17
00:01:45,750 --> 00:01:50,400
Annulled. l'll have something to say about that and so will King.

18
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:50,840
l expect him to.

19
00:01:54,150 --> 00:01:55,850
The vittles. Come in. Come in.

20
00:01:55,850 --> 00:01:59,030
l told you not to bring any food in here.

21
00:01:59,030 --> 00:02:00,690
Now wait a minute. This isn't for you.

22
00:02:00,690 --> 00:02:02,340
Put it down here.

23
00:02:11,170 --> 00:02:13,570
Smart, aren't you? So subtle.

24
00:02:13,570 --> 00:02:14,940
Strategy, my dear.

25
00:02:14,940 --> 00:02:17,590
Was it strategy sending those gorillas to drag me away...

26
00:02:17,590 --> 00:02:19,230
and I can just sit in peace.

27
00:02:19,230 --> 00:02:21,650
Your idea of strategy is to use a lead pipe.

28
00:02:21,650 --> 00:02:23,800
l've won many arguments that way.

29
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:27,380
Besides not liking him, you haven't got a thing against King.

30
00:02:27,380 --> 00:02:30,190
-He's a fake.  -He's one of the best flyers in the country.

31
00:02:30,190 --> 00:02:33,020
He's no good. You married him because l said not to.

32
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:33,910
You're always telling me what not to do.

33
00:02:33,910 --> 00:02:37,150
Because you've always been a stubborn idiot.

34
00:02:37,470 --> 00:02:39,710
l come from a long line of stubborn idiots.

35
00:02:39,710 --> 00:02:42,710
Don't shout so. You may work up an appetite.

36
00:02:42,710 --> 00:02:45,470
l'll shout if l want to! l'll scream if l want to!

37
00:02:45,470 --> 00:02:46,700
All right, scream.

38
00:02:46,700 --> 00:02:50,020
Let me off this boat or l'll break every piece of furniture in here!

39
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:55,070
Have a nice piece of juicy steak. You don't have to eat it.

40
00:02:55,070 --> 00:02:56,980
Just smell it. lt's a poem.

41
00:03:05,700 --> 00:03:06,260
Ellie

42
00:03:06,870 --> 00:03:07,790
Ellie

43
00:03:09,720 --> 00:03:11,930
Ellie! Ellie!

44
00:03:14,130 --> 00:03:17,570
Lower the boats! Lower the boats! Catch her! Catch her!

45
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:19,900
Come on, men! Come on!

46
00:03:24,370 --> 00:03:25,320
She got away, sir.

47
00:03:25,320 --> 00:03:27,800
Of course, she's too smart for you.

48
00:03:28,250 --> 00:03:30,660
Send a wireless to the Lovington Detective Agency.

49
00:03:30,660 --> 00:03:31,950
"Daughter escaped again.

50
00:03:31,950 --> 00:03:34,860
"Watch roads, airports and train stations in Miami."

51
00:03:34,860 --> 00:03:40,720
All aboard! Palm Beach, Savannah, Jacksonville...

52
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:43,070
...New York, Philadelphia.

53
00:03:43,070 --> 00:03:46,250
We're wasting our time. lmagine Ellie Andrews riding on a bus.

54
00:03:46,250 --> 00:03:48,010
l told the old man it was bunk.

55
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:49,630
Ticket for New York, please.

56
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,390
-Here's your ticket.  -Thank you very much.

57
00:03:58,760 --> 00:04:01,000
Oh! Thank you. Thank you.

58
00:04:05,590 --> 00:04:07,860
Hey! What's going on here? l'd like to use that phone.

59
00:04:07,930 --> 00:04:10,650
Go away. This is history in the making.

60
00:04:10,710 --> 00:04:13,840
-What?  -There's a man biting a dog in there.

61
00:04:16,190 --> 00:04:18,130
l can't stand this any longer.

62
00:04:18,520 --> 00:04:20,870
ln a pig's eye, you will.

63
00:04:22,870 --> 00:04:24,960
Hey! Listen monkey face, when you fired me,

64
00:04:24,960 --> 00:04:26,100
you fired the best news hound...

65
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:28,470
your filthy scandal sheet ever had.

66
00:04:28,770 --> 00:04:32,180
Say listen! You wouldn't know a newspaper story if it kicked you in the pants.

67
00:04:32,180 --> 00:04:33,880
Yeah, yeah she'll get all your copy.

68
00:04:33,880 --> 00:04:36,300
Why didn't you tell me you were gonna write it in Greek?

69
00:04:36,300 --> 00:04:37,570
l'd start a new department.

70
00:04:37,570 --> 00:04:40,170
That was free verse, you gas house palooka.

71
00:04:40,170 --> 00:04:43,210
What was free about it? lt cost this paper a gob of dough.

72
00:04:43,210 --> 00:04:45,020
And it's not going to cost us any more!

73
00:04:45,020 --> 00:04:46,050
Gordon.

74
00:04:46,050 --> 00:04:48,320
Did you know he reversed the charge on that call?

75
00:04:48,320 --> 00:04:50,840
What? Why you....

76
00:04:50,840 --> 00:04:53,510
Say listen, you,  when you get back to New York,

77
00:04:53,510 --> 00:04:55,730
you keep far away from this office.

78
00:04:55,730 --> 00:04:58,610
You're fired. You don't work here anymore and you never will.

79
00:05:01,350 --> 00:05:03,010
What'd he say?

80
00:05:04,960 --> 00:05:08,100
Oh, so you're changing your tune?

81
00:05:10,150 --> 00:05:11,560
You're late with your apologies.

82
00:05:11,650 --> 00:05:13,230
l wouldn't go back to work for you

83
00:05:13,230 --> 00:05:15,170
if you begged me on your hands and knees!

84
00:05:15,270 --> 00:05:17,090
l hope this'll be a lesson to you.

85
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:21,030
Did we tell that baby?

86
00:05:21,090 --> 00:05:24,220
-We don't need anymore of his lip.  -You told him, Pete.

87
00:05:24,290 --> 00:05:27,510
l guess he knows now, how l feel about his job.

88
00:05:27,510 --> 00:05:28,900
l bet he does, too.

89
00:05:28,900 --> 00:05:31,050
ls my chariot ready?

90
00:05:31,050 --> 00:05:34,840
Your chariot awaiteth withouteth, mighty King.

91
00:05:36,390 --> 00:05:39,140
-Lead on, sire.  -Make way for the king.

92
00:05:39,140 --> 00:05:40,570
Make way for the king.

93
00:05:40,570 --> 00:05:42,590
Long live the king.

94
00:06:06,190 --> 00:06:08,810
Make yourself comfortable with a pleasant pillow.

95
00:06:09,170 --> 00:06:10,210
Pillow, sir?

96
00:06:18,290 --> 00:06:21,150
Hey! Driver! lf you'll be good enough to move those newspapers,

97
00:06:21,150 --> 00:06:22,760
l'll have a seat.

98
00:06:31,980 --> 00:06:33,480
Hey, wait a minute!

99
00:06:37,800 --> 00:06:39,250
What do you think you're doing?

100
00:06:39,250 --> 00:06:42,860
The papers. The papers. What's the idea of throwing them out?

101
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:45,600
The papers? lt's a long story, my friend.

102
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:48,440
l never did like the idea of sitting on newspapers.

103
00:06:48,440 --> 00:06:51,800
l did it once, and all the headlines came off on my white pants.

104
00:06:51,800 --> 00:06:55,500
lt actually happened. Nobody bought a paper that day.

105
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:59,200
They followed me all over town and read the news off the seat of my pants.

106
00:06:59,200 --> 00:07:04,020
A fresh guy. What you need is a good sock on the nose.

107
00:07:06,330 --> 00:07:10,300
Listen partner, you may not like my nose, but l do.

108
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:12,290
l always wear it out in the open so...

109
00:07:12,290 --> 00:07:15,200
...if anybody wants to take a sock at it, they can do it.

110
00:07:16,980 --> 00:07:18,360
Oh, yeah?

111
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:22,580
Now, that's a brilliant answer. Why didn't l think of it?

112
00:07:22,580 --> 00:07:24,930
Our conversation could have been over long ago.

113
00:07:24,930 --> 00:07:26,250
Oh, yeah?

114
00:07:26,900 --> 00:07:29,270
lf you keep that up, we won't get anywhere.

115
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:31,150
Oh, yeah?

116
00:07:32,550 --> 00:07:35,610
You got me. Yeah!

117
00:07:43,910 --> 00:07:47,910
Excuse me, lady. But that upon which you sit is mine.

118
00:07:48,970 --> 00:07:50,570
l beg your pardon?

119
00:07:50,570 --> 00:07:53,420
Now listen, l put up a stiff fight for that seat.

120
00:07:53,420 --> 00:07:56,860
So, if it's just the same to you, scram.

121
00:07:57,530 --> 00:08:00,010
Driver, are these seats reserved?

122
00:08:00,010 --> 00:08:03,340
-No. First come, first serve.  -Thank you.

123
00:08:03,340 --> 00:08:07,170
Hey, driver, these seats accommodate two people, don't they?

124
00:08:07,170 --> 00:08:09,160
Maybe they do, maybe they don't.

125
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:10,040
Thank you.

126
00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:14,240
Move over.

127
00:08:16,150 --> 00:08:19,000
This is a "maybe they do."

128
00:08:25,900 --> 00:08:28,580
lf you'd ask me real nice, l might put that bag up there for you.

129
00:08:47,940 --> 00:08:50,400
Next time you drop in, bring your folks.

130
00:09:11,100 --> 00:09:13,090
Get some! Come on, everybody!

131
00:09:13,870 --> 00:09:15,100
Hot dogs, folks!

132
00:09:18,390 --> 00:09:22,040
Rest station, 15 minutes. We'll only be here 15 minutes.

133
00:09:22,470 --> 00:09:23,610
Red hot coffee!

134
00:09:24,560 --> 00:09:25,590
Right around there.

135
00:09:25,590 --> 00:09:28,470
Get the red hot coffee! Hot dogs!

136
00:09:28,540 --> 00:09:31,040
Can't enjoy the ride unless you eat!

137
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:15,000
He got away.

138
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:18,340
l found myself in the middle of brush and no sign of the skunk.

139
00:10:18,440 --> 00:10:20,760
l don't know what you're raving about, young man.

140
00:10:20,760 --> 00:10:25,120
-Furthermore, l'm not interested.  -Well of all the....

141
00:10:25,120 --> 00:10:27,510
Maybe you'll be interested to know your bag is gone.

142
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:30,050
Oh! My heavens! lt's gone!

143
00:10:30,120 --> 00:10:31,870
l knew you'd catch on eventually.

144
00:10:33,350 --> 00:10:36,420
-What am l going to do now?  -Don't tell me your ticket was in it.

145
00:10:37,050 --> 00:10:40,270
No, got that all right. But not my money.

146
00:10:40,270 --> 00:10:42,280
All l have here is $4.

147
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:44,050
You can wire home for money in Jacksonville.

148
00:10:44,050 --> 00:10:45,290
No, l can't.

149
00:10:46,070 --> 00:10:48,850
-Yes, l guess l will.  -l'll tell the driver about your bag.

150
00:10:48,850 --> 00:10:51,300
No! Thank you, l'd rather you didn't.

151
00:10:51,710 --> 00:10:54,530
Don't be a fool. You've lost your bag. The company will make you good.

152
00:10:54,530 --> 00:10:57,230
-What's your name?  -l don't want it reported!

153
00:10:57,230 --> 00:10:59,690
That's ridiculous. The company will take care of it.

154
00:10:59,690 --> 00:11:04,290
Can you understand English? Would you please keep out of my affairs?

155
00:11:04,290 --> 00:11:06,310
l want to be left alone.

156
00:11:10,490 --> 00:11:12,470
Well, you ungrateful brat.

157
00:11:12,470 --> 00:11:14,030
Board!

158
00:11:14,030 --> 00:11:15,850
All aboard!

159
00:11:18,520 --> 00:11:19,990
Board!

160
00:12:58,030 --> 00:13:00,240
Jacksonville, 30 minutes for breakfast.

161
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:03,250
Only 30 minutes for breakfast.

162
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:08,970
Just 30 minutes. That's all. No more.

163
00:13:34,730 --> 00:13:36,320
l'm so sorry.

164
00:13:37,670 --> 00:13:38,920
Silly, isn't it?

165
00:13:40,300 --> 00:13:42,270
Why, everybody's gone!

166
00:13:45,900 --> 00:13:48,370
Thank you for that, very much.

167
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:52,260
-We're in Jacksonville, aren't we?  -Yes.

168
00:13:55,780 --> 00:13:57,510
That was foolish of me.

169
00:13:58,250 --> 00:14:01,210
Why didn't you shove me away?

170
00:14:01,480 --> 00:14:05,440
l hated to wake you up. You look kind of pretty asleep.

171
00:14:06,410 --> 00:14:08,160
How about some breakfast?

172
00:14:08,230 --> 00:14:12,670
No, no, thank you. No, l'm going to the Windsor Hotel.

173
00:14:13,710 --> 00:14:16,740
Windsor? You'll never make it in time. We leave in a half an hour.

174
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:19,880
Oh, no, they'll wait for me.

175
00:14:22,540 --> 00:14:26,420
Driver, l'm going to be a few minutes late. Be sure to wait for me.

176
00:14:26,420 --> 00:14:28,270
Oh, yeah?

177
00:14:28,270 --> 00:14:29,400
Yes.

178
00:14:51,970 --> 00:14:53,370
Where's the bus to New York?

179
00:14:53,440 --> 00:14:55,160
lt left about 20 minutes ago.

180
00:14:55,710 --> 00:14:59,510
But that's ridiculous. l was on that bus. l told them to wait.

181
00:14:59,580 --> 00:15:01,440
l'm sorry, miss, but it's gone.

182
00:15:02,430 --> 00:15:06,690
Good morning. Remember me? l'm the fellow you slept on last night.

183
00:15:08,700 --> 00:15:11,070
Seems to me, l've already thanked you for that.

184
00:15:11,740 --> 00:15:13,100
What time's the next bus?

185
00:15:13,100 --> 00:15:14,060
8:00 tonight.

186
00:15:14,720 --> 00:15:17,880
8:00? That's 12 hours.

187
00:15:17,880 --> 00:15:19,420
Sorry, miss.

188
00:15:20,710 --> 00:15:23,200
What's the matter? Wouldn't the old meanies wait for you?

189
00:15:23,490 --> 00:15:25,730
Why are you so excited? You missed it, too.

190
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:27,420
Yeah, l missed it too.

191
00:15:28,680 --> 00:15:31,330
Don't tell me you did it on my account.

192
00:15:32,170 --> 00:15:35,910
l hope you haven't any idea that what happened last night is....

193
00:15:36,360 --> 00:15:39,720
Now look here, young man, you needn't concern yourself about me.

194
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:40,970
l can take care of myself.

195
00:15:41,040 --> 00:15:45,160
You're doing a pretty sloppy job of it. Here's your ticket.

196
00:15:45,680 --> 00:15:46,600
My ticket?

197
00:15:46,700 --> 00:15:47,630
l found it on the seat.

198
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:56,740
Thank you. lt must have fallen out of my purse.

199
00:15:58,540 --> 00:16:00,230
You'll never get away with it, Miss Andrews.

200
00:16:02,860 --> 00:16:05,540
-What are you talking about?  -I said you won't get away with it.

201
00:16:05,610 --> 00:16:07,850
Your father will stop you before you get halfway to New York.

202
00:16:09,900 --> 00:16:12,070
You must have me confused with someone else.

203
00:16:12,070 --> 00:16:14,410
Quit kidding. lt's all over the front page.

204
00:16:20,300 --> 00:16:22,570
l've always been curious to know...

205
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:26,320
...what kind of a girl would marry a front-page aviator like King Westley.

206
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:29,080
Take my advice. Grab the next bus back to Miami.

207
00:16:29,080 --> 00:16:30,150
That guy's a phoney.

208
00:16:32,490 --> 00:16:34,280
l didn't ask for your advice.

209
00:16:35,400 --> 00:16:37,190
That's right. You didn't.

210
00:16:37,900 --> 00:16:40,860
Wait, you're not going to notify my father, are you?

211
00:16:40,940 --> 00:16:42,020
What for?

212
00:16:43,400 --> 00:16:45,500
You probably could get some money out of him.

213
00:16:45,860 --> 00:16:46,940
l never thought of that.

214
00:16:47,080 --> 00:16:49,140
Listen, if you promise not to do it,

215
00:16:49,150 --> 00:16:50,750
l'll pay you, I'll pay you as much as he will.

216
00:16:50,850 --> 00:16:52,850
You won't gain a thing by giving me up.

217
00:16:52,850 --> 00:16:54,630
as long as l'm willing to make it worth your while.

218
00:16:54,730 --> 00:16:57,410
l've got to get to New York without being stopped.

219
00:16:57,410 --> 00:16:59,410
lt's terribly important to me.

220
00:16:59,610 --> 00:17:01,390
l'd pay you now, only...

221
00:17:01,460 --> 00:17:04,050
...the only thing all l had when l jumped off the yacht was a watch.

222
00:17:04,120 --> 00:17:05,490
l had to pawn it to get these clothes.

223
00:17:05,690 --> 00:17:08,750
Look, l'll give you my address. And you can contact me in New York.

224
00:17:08,820 --> 00:17:10,000
Never mind.

225
00:17:11,490 --> 00:17:13,840
You know l had you pegged right from the jump.

226
00:17:14,570 --> 00:17:16,320
Just the spoiled brat of a rich father.

227
00:17:16,320 --> 00:17:18,200
The only way you get anything is to buy it, isn't it?

228
00:17:18,790 --> 00:17:21,190
You're in a jam and all you can think of is your money.

229
00:17:21,190 --> 00:17:22,510
lt never fails, does it?

230
00:17:23,370 --> 00:17:25,270
Ever hear of the word "humility"?

231
00:17:25,270 --> 00:17:27,290
No, you wouldn't.

232
00:17:27,290 --> 00:17:29,010
I guess lt never occurred to you to say...

233
00:17:29,340 --> 00:17:31,120
..."Please, Mister, l'm in trouble. Will you help me?"

234
00:17:31,790 --> 00:17:34,200
No, that'd bring you down off your high horse.

235
00:17:34,830 --> 00:17:36,690
Let me tell you something to ease your mind.

236
00:17:36,690 --> 00:17:38,500
You don't have to worry about me.

237
00:17:38,780 --> 00:17:41,000
l'm not interested in your money or your problem.

238
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:44,340
You, King Westley, your father. You're all a lot of hooey to me.

239
00:17:51,740 --> 00:17:53,370
You send telegrams here?

240
00:17:54,010 --> 00:17:56,090
l'm just fine, thanks. And how are you?

241
00:18:00,320 --> 00:18:03,410
"To Joe Gordon, in care of New York Mail, New York.

242
00:18:03,410 --> 00:18:08,150
"Am l laughing. The biggest scoop of the year just dropped in my lap.

243
00:18:08,150 --> 00:18:11,260
"l know where Ellen Andrews is." No, do you really?

244
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,750
Go on. Go on. Send the telegram.

245
00:18:14,750 --> 00:18:18,920
"How would you like to have the story? You big tub of, of...."

246
00:18:19,550 --> 00:18:20,710
Mush. Mush.

247
00:18:20,710 --> 00:18:23,210
"Tub of mush. Well, try and get it.

248
00:18:23,210 --> 00:18:26,970
"What l said about never writing another line for you still goes.

249
00:18:26,970 --> 00:18:29,390
"Are you burning? Peter Warne."

250
00:18:29,390 --> 00:18:31,060
That'll be $2.60.

251
00:18:31,060 --> 00:18:32,990
-Send it collect.  -Collect?

252
00:18:32,990 --> 00:18:34,640
Collect.

253
00:18:37,790 --> 00:18:40,580
Bus leaving for Savannah, Charleston,

254
00:18:40,580 --> 00:18:43,090
Columbia, Greensboro, Richmond...

255
00:18:43,090 --> 00:18:47,650
...Washington, Baltimore, Philadelphia, New York....

256
00:19:14,230 --> 00:19:17,790
Hi, sister. All alone? My name's Shapeley.

257
00:19:17,790 --> 00:19:19,580
May as well get acquainted, it's a long trip.

258
00:19:19,580 --> 00:19:22,180
Gets tiresome. Especially for somebody like you.

259
00:19:22,180 --> 00:19:23,940
You look like you've got class.

260
00:19:23,940 --> 00:19:28,670
Yes, with a capital "K". l'm the guy that knows class when he sees it.

261
00:19:28,670 --> 00:19:32,320
Believe you me. Ask any of the boys. They'll tell you.

262
00:19:32,320 --> 00:19:34,690
Shapeley sure knows how to pick them.

263
00:19:34,690 --> 00:19:37,760
Yes,sir. Shapeley's the name and that's the way l like them.

264
00:19:37,760 --> 00:19:39,510
You made no mistake sitting next to me.

265
00:19:39,510 --> 00:19:41,300
Just between most girls you meet on the bus...

266
00:19:41,300 --> 00:19:43,270
...ain't nothing to write home to the wife about.

267
00:19:43,270 --> 00:19:45,920
You gotta be awful careful who you hit it up with.

268
00:19:45,920 --> 00:19:48,390
as well as you can't be too particular, neither.

269
00:19:49,270 --> 00:19:51,080
What's the matter, you ain't saying much?

270
00:19:51,720 --> 00:19:54,410
Seems to me you're doing excellently without any assistance.

271
00:19:56,260 --> 00:19:57,710
That's pretty good.

272
00:19:57,720 --> 00:20:00,630
"Seems to me you're doing excellently without any assistance."

273
00:20:01,310 --> 00:20:04,100
Well shut my big, nasty mouth.

274
00:20:05,240 --> 00:20:06,840
Looks like you're one up on me.

275
00:20:06,840 --> 00:20:10,210
You know there's nothing l like better than to meet a high-class mama...

276
00:20:10,210 --> 00:20:14,640
...that can snap back at you. The colder they are, the hotter they get.

277
00:20:14,640 --> 00:20:15,850
That's what l always say.

278
00:20:15,850 --> 00:20:17,940
Yes, sir.

279
00:20:17,940 --> 00:20:22,420
When a cold mama gets hot, boy how she sizzles.

280
00:20:24,380 --> 00:20:26,000
Now you're just my type.

281
00:20:26,420 --> 00:20:29,390
Believe me, sister, l could go for you in a big way.

282
00:20:29,970 --> 00:20:34,240
"Fun-on-the-side Shapeley," they call me. With accent on the "fun".

283
00:20:34,240 --> 00:20:35,450
Believe you me.

284
00:20:35,450 --> 00:20:39,010
Believe you me, you bore me to distraction.

285
00:20:41,030 --> 00:20:43,180
Looks like you're two up on me now.

286
00:20:43,710 --> 00:20:44,530
Hey, you.

287
00:20:46,280 --> 00:20:49,620
-There's a seat over there for you.  -What's the idea?

288
00:20:49,620 --> 00:20:52,620
l'd like to sit next to my wife, if you don't mind.

289
00:20:53,200 --> 00:20:54,960
-Your wife?  -Yes.

290
00:20:55,870 --> 00:20:56,930
Come on.Come on.

291
00:20:57,420 --> 00:21:01,130
Oh! Yeah. Sure, sure, excuse me. You know, l was just....

292
00:21:01,130 --> 00:21:04,600
Sure. Excuse me, miss. l was just trying to make things pleasant.

293
00:21:05,690 --> 00:21:06,640
Excuse me, l....

294
00:21:06,640 --> 00:21:09,430
l didn't mean anything, Doc.

295
00:21:10,850 --> 00:21:12,690
-No offence, Doc.  -No.

296
00:21:18,960 --> 00:21:22,440
lf you promise not to snap my head off, l'd like to thank you.

297
00:21:22,510 --> 00:21:27,150
Forget it. l didn't do it for you. His voice gets on my nerves.

298
00:21:32,920 --> 00:21:34,770
What'd you do all day?

299
00:21:36,450 --> 00:21:39,520
Ran in and out of doorways. Trying to keep out of the rain.

300
00:21:42,950 --> 00:21:45,010
Your clothes are all wet.

301
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:48,230
Here.

302
00:21:49,030 --> 00:21:51,790
You're as helpless as a baby.

303
00:21:51,960 --> 00:21:52,890
Thank you.

304
00:21:53,210 --> 00:21:55,680
Here you are, folks. Cigars, cigarettes,

305
00:21:55,680 --> 00:21:57,780
chewing gum, candy, magazines.

306
00:21:58,040 --> 00:21:59,320
Here, boy.

307
00:22:01,530 --> 00:22:03,600
-Yes, ma'am.  -A box of chocolates, please.

308
00:22:03,670 --> 00:22:06,340
-Never mind. She doesn't want it.  -But the lady said....

309
00:22:06,340 --> 00:22:08,720
-Of course, l do. What do you mean?  -Beat it.

310
00:22:09,430 --> 00:22:12,150
Well, you've got your nerve. Here, boy!

311
00:22:13,940 --> 00:22:15,440
$1 .60.

312
00:22:16,500 --> 00:22:18,660
You had $4 last night.

313
00:22:18,660 --> 00:22:21,240
How will you get to New York at this rate?

314
00:22:21,370 --> 00:22:23,130
That's none of your business.

315
00:22:24,560 --> 00:22:26,830
You're on a budget from now on.

316
00:22:27,220 --> 00:22:29,680
-Just a minute. You can't--  -Shut up.

317
00:22:51,220 --> 00:22:55,270
-What's the matter, officer?  -Bridge washed out.

318
00:22:55,270 --> 00:22:57,090
Looks like we can't get through till morning.

319
00:22:57,160 --> 00:23:00,350
lf any passengers want a place to sleep...

320
00:23:00,350 --> 00:23:01,950
...you'll find an auto camp up yonder a piece.

321
00:23:02,680 --> 00:23:05,270
-Where?  -Right over there. See those lights?

322
00:23:05,500 --> 00:23:07,540
-Oh, yeah.  -Dyke's Auto camp.

323
00:23:07,610 --> 00:23:09,620
All right, thanks. Hey, brat.

324
00:23:10,620 --> 00:23:11,860
Are you talking to me?

325
00:23:11,930 --> 00:23:14,800
Yeah. Come on, we're stopping here for the night.

326
00:23:30,570 --> 00:23:33,800
Hey! Come on, come on, we're all set.

327
00:23:44,950 --> 00:23:48,490
Good evening. Hope you and your husband rest comfortable.

328
00:23:56,880 --> 00:24:00,320
Come on! Come on! What are you going to do, stay out there all night?

329
00:24:21,890 --> 00:24:23,690
You're clever, these means.

330
00:24:23,690 --> 00:24:25,390
Yeah, it's a gift.

331
00:24:27,510 --> 00:24:29,960
l just had the unpleasant sensation

332
00:24:29,960 --> 00:24:32,830
of hearing you referred to as my husband.

333
00:24:32,830 --> 00:24:36,820
Oh, yeah. l forgot to tell you about that. l registered as Mr. and Mrs.

334
00:24:37,810 --> 00:24:38,710
Oh! You did?

335
00:24:40,610 --> 00:24:43,480
What am l expected to do? Leap for joy?

336
00:24:43,480 --> 00:24:45,930
l kind of half expected you to thank me.

337
00:24:46,870 --> 00:24:49,770
Your ego is absolutely colossal.

338
00:24:49,850 --> 00:24:52,430
Yeah, it's not bad. How's yours?

339
00:24:59,660 --> 00:25:04,270
You know, compared to you, my friend Shapeley's an amateur.

340
00:25:05,130 --> 00:25:08,170
Just whatever gave you any idea l'd stand for this?

341
00:25:08,780 --> 00:25:12,520
Now wait a minute. Let's get this straightened out right now.

342
00:25:12,520 --> 00:25:15,890
lf you're nursing any silly notion that l'm interested in you, forget it.

343
00:25:15,980 --> 00:25:17,840
You're just a headline to me.

344
00:25:18,640 --> 00:25:20,210
A headline?

345
00:25:21,870 --> 00:25:24,280
You're not a newspaper man, are you?

346
00:25:24,280 --> 00:25:26,190
Chalk up one for your side.

347
00:25:27,260 --> 00:25:30,600
Now listen. You want to get to King Westley, don't you?

348
00:25:30,600 --> 00:25:35,160
All right, l'm here to help you. What l want is your story.

349
00:25:35,160 --> 00:25:39,840
Exclusive. A day-to-day account. All about your mad fight to happiness.

350
00:25:39,950 --> 00:25:43,840
l need that story. Between you and me, l've got to have it.

351
00:25:47,550 --> 00:25:49,960
lsn't that just too cute.

352
00:25:51,090 --> 00:25:54,040
There's a brain behind that face of yours, isn't there?

353
00:25:55,010 --> 00:25:59,480
You've got everything nicely figured out for yourself. lncluding this.

354
00:25:59,480 --> 00:26:03,040
This? Well, that's a matter of simple mathematics.

355
00:26:03,040 --> 00:26:07,220
These cabins cost $2 a night. l'm very sorry to inform you, wifey dear...

356
00:26:07,220 --> 00:26:10,700
...but the family purse won't stand for our having separate establishment.

357
00:26:17,600 --> 00:26:22,140
Thank you. Thank you very much, sir. You've been very kind.

358
00:26:22,460 --> 00:26:24,420
lt's all right with me. Go on out in the storm.

359
00:26:24,420 --> 00:26:26,620
But l'm going to follow you.

360
00:26:28,130 --> 00:26:30,560
And if you get tough,

361
00:26:30,560 --> 00:26:32,990
l'll just have to turn you over to your old man. Right now.

362
00:26:32,990 --> 00:26:36,310
Savvy? That's my whole plot in a nutshell.

363
00:26:37,470 --> 00:26:39,960
A simple story for simple people.

364
00:26:40,570 --> 00:26:43,030
You behave yourself, l'll see you get to King Westley.

365
00:26:43,130 --> 00:26:46,130
lf not, l'll just have to spill the beans to Papa.

366
00:26:47,390 --> 00:26:51,010
Now, which of these beds do you prefer?

367
00:26:51,680 --> 00:26:54,070
This one? All right.

368
00:27:17,490 --> 00:27:21,020
That, l suppose, makes everything quite all right.

369
00:27:21,020 --> 00:27:22,250
This?

370
00:27:25,530 --> 00:27:29,060
Well, l like privacy when l retire. Yes, l'm very delicate in that respect.

371
00:27:29,060 --> 00:27:31,110
Prying eyes annoy me.

372
00:27:35,720 --> 00:27:37,600
Behold the walls of Jericho.

373
00:27:37,990 --> 00:27:41,470
Maybe not as thick as the ones that Joshua blew down with his trumpet.

374
00:27:41,540 --> 00:27:42,970
But a lot safer.

375
00:27:43,050 --> 00:27:46,010
You see, l have no trumpet.

376
00:27:46,570 --> 00:27:48,940
Now to show you my heart's in the right place...

377
00:27:48,940 --> 00:27:51,320
...l'll give you my best pair of pyjamas.

378
00:27:53,570 --> 00:27:56,190
Do you mind joining the lsraelites?

379
00:27:56,870 --> 00:27:59,720
You don't want to join the lsraelites?

380
00:28:00,100 --> 00:28:04,870
All right. Perhaps you're interested in how a man undresses.

381
00:28:04,870 --> 00:28:07,450
There's a funny thing about that. Quite a study in psychology.

382
00:28:07,450 --> 00:28:08,480
No two men do it alike.

383
00:28:10,140 --> 00:28:13,720
l once knew a man who kept his hat on until he was completely undressed.

384
00:28:13,720 --> 00:28:15,780
Now he made a picture.

385
00:28:15,780 --> 00:28:19,740
Years later, his secret came out. He wore a toupee.

386
00:28:21,300 --> 00:28:23,020
l have a method all my own.

387
00:28:24,030 --> 00:28:27,720
lf you'll notice, the coat came first. Then the tie. Then the shirt.

388
00:28:28,360 --> 00:28:32,830
Now, according to Hoyle, after that the pants should be next.

389
00:28:32,830 --> 00:28:34,380
There's where l'm different.

390
00:28:34,850 --> 00:28:36,490
l go for the shoes next.

391
00:28:37,140 --> 00:28:39,520
First the right. Then the left.

392
00:28:41,110 --> 00:28:45,050
After that, it's every man for himself.

393
00:29:08,450 --> 00:29:10,100
Still with me, brat?

394
00:29:13,760 --> 00:29:15,540
Don't be a sucker.

395
00:29:17,050 --> 00:29:19,730
A good night's rest will do you a lot of good.

396
00:29:19,730 --> 00:29:21,180
Besides, you got nothing to worry about.

397
00:29:21,850 --> 00:29:24,500
The walls of Jericho will protect you from the big bad wolf.

398
00:29:39,650 --> 00:29:44,010
"Who's afraid of the big bad wolf?. The big bad wolf

399
00:29:44,010 --> 00:29:45,310
"The big bad wolf

400
00:29:45,830 --> 00:29:51,450
"She's afraid of the big bad wolf Tra, la, la, la, la"

401
00:29:53,870 --> 00:29:55,980
Would you mind please, putting out the light?

402
00:29:56,500 --> 00:29:57,640
No, not at all.

403
00:30:38,400 --> 00:30:41,330
l wish you'd take those things off the walls of Jericho.

404
00:30:41,470 --> 00:30:42,780
Oh! Excuse me.

405
00:31:09,810 --> 00:31:11,570
By the way, what's your name?

406
00:31:12,920 --> 00:31:13,510
What's that?

407
00:31:14,390 --> 00:31:15,400
Who are you?

408
00:31:17,140 --> 00:31:18,350
Who, me?

409
00:31:19,540 --> 00:31:22,220
l'm the whippoorwill that cries in the night.

410
00:31:22,800 --> 00:31:26,830
l'm the soft morning breeze that caresses your lovely face.

411
00:31:27,320 --> 00:31:29,230
You've got a name, haven't you?

412
00:31:29,880 --> 00:31:32,780
Yeah, l got a name. Peter Warne.

413
00:31:33,660 --> 00:31:35,070
Peter Warne.

414
00:31:36,700 --> 00:31:38,300
l don't like it.

415
00:31:38,620 --> 00:31:41,560
Don't let it bother you. You're giving it back to me in the morning.

416
00:31:44,640 --> 00:31:46,200
Pleased to meet you, Mr. Warne.

417
00:31:46,690 --> 00:31:50,140
The pleasure is all mine, Mrs. Warne.

418
00:32:10,480 --> 00:32:13,200
-Another message, sir.  -What is it? What is it? What is it?

419
00:32:13,270 --> 00:32:15,980
lt's from Charleston. "Checking every northbound train.

420
00:32:15,980 --> 00:32:18,730
"Also assigned 20 operators to watch main highways.

421
00:32:18,730 --> 00:32:21,680
"No sign of her yet. Will continue to do all possible.

422
00:32:21,680 --> 00:32:23,320
"Signed, Lovington Detective Agency."

423
00:32:23,590 --> 00:32:25,530
lt's just the same as all the others.

424
00:32:26,890 --> 00:32:30,140
-Yes, sir?  -l said l was in a hurry to get to New York.

425
00:32:30,140 --> 00:32:31,890
-What are we crawling for?  -l got it wide open, sir.

426
00:32:31,890 --> 00:32:33,750
-All right, step on it.  -Yes, sir.

427
00:32:34,810 --> 00:32:36,410
l hope she's all right, sir.

428
00:32:36,410 --> 00:32:40,210
All right? Of course, she's all right. What could happen to her?

429
00:32:40,640 --> 00:32:43,070
-Nothing, sir.  -Then shut up about it.

430
00:33:08,380 --> 00:33:10,040
Hello?

431
00:33:11,650 --> 00:33:13,070
Hey, mister.

432
00:33:17,550 --> 00:33:18,820
Hello.

433
00:33:18,820 --> 00:33:20,590
What's the matter, you not up yet?

434
00:33:21,000 --> 00:33:24,290
-What time is it?  -8:00. Here.

435
00:33:26,280 --> 00:33:28,230
Oh! lt's a toothbrush, thanks.

436
00:33:28,750 --> 00:33:31,590
My dress, you had it pressed.

437
00:33:31,820 --> 00:33:33,760
Come on. Come on. Breakfast will be ready soon.

438
00:33:33,870 --> 00:33:36,100
You sweet thing. Where'd you get it pressed?

439
00:33:36,170 --> 00:33:38,510
Say listen, l'll count to 10. lf you're not out of bed by then...

440
00:33:38,510 --> 00:33:41,300
...I'm coming over here and l'll drag you out myself.

441
00:33:41,300 --> 00:33:43,870
-One, two, three, four, five....  -l really think you would!

442
00:33:43,870 --> 00:33:45,010
l'm out! l'm out!

443
00:33:45,010 --> 00:33:47,700
l'm out! l'm out! I'm out!

444
00:33:48,190 --> 00:33:51,570
You'll find the showers just behind the second cottage.

445
00:33:52,900 --> 00:33:54,730
Outside?

446
00:33:54,730 --> 00:33:57,420
Surely outside. All the best homes have them outside.

447
00:34:00,100 --> 00:34:02,630
l can't go out like this.

448
00:34:02,630 --> 00:34:05,110
-Like what?  -Like this. l have no robe.

449
00:34:05,110 --> 00:34:07,420
Here, use mine.

450
00:34:08,310 --> 00:34:09,290
Oh, thanks.

451
00:34:09,910 --> 00:34:11,010
Come on. Come on. Make it snappy.

452
00:34:11,010 --> 00:34:12,990
Wait, it's not my fault. You got the sleeve.

453
00:34:13,590 --> 00:34:16,650
-Here. Here are my puppets.  -Thanks.

454
00:34:18,840 --> 00:34:21,590
Where'd you say the showers were?

455
00:34:21,590 --> 00:34:22,670
Here's a towel.

456
00:34:24,450 --> 00:34:25,350
Thank you.

457
00:34:27,280 --> 00:34:28,930
You're kind of little, aren't you?

458
00:34:29,900 --> 00:34:31,100
Where's the shower?

459
00:34:31,100 --> 00:34:33,320
Your hair's cute like that. You should never comb it.

460
00:34:33,320 --> 00:34:35,210
l'll find it myself.

461
00:35:08,830 --> 00:35:10,320
Are the showers in there?

462
00:35:10,460 --> 00:35:12,320
They ain't out here.

463
00:35:12,320 --> 00:35:13,320
Thank you.

464
00:35:17,530 --> 00:35:20,350
Can't a body have a little privacy around here?

465
00:35:25,150 --> 00:35:28,380
You want a shower around here, you'll stand in line.

466
00:35:39,270 --> 00:35:42,330
Hi, sister. You remember me, Shapeley?

467
00:35:42,330 --> 00:35:44,220
Say, l'm sorry about last night.

468
00:35:44,220 --> 00:35:47,090
Didn't know you was married to that guy. You should've told me right off.

469
00:35:57,740 --> 00:35:59,370
High time you got back.

470
00:35:59,510 --> 00:36:01,930
Oh, l met some very interesting women at the showers.

471
00:36:02,000 --> 00:36:05,680
We got chatting about this and that. You know how time flies.

472
00:36:08,570 --> 00:36:09,960
Come on. Come on. Sit down.

473
00:36:12,990 --> 00:36:15,310
My, my. Scrambled eggs.

474
00:36:15,310 --> 00:36:19,490
Egg. One egg. One donut, black coffee.

475
00:36:19,490 --> 00:36:21,260
That's your ration till lunch.

476
00:36:21,260 --> 00:36:22,320
Any complaints?

477
00:36:22,320 --> 00:36:24,070
No. No complaints.

478
00:36:24,070 --> 00:36:27,130
l'd have cream for your coffee, but l'd be buying a whole pint.

479
00:36:27,130 --> 00:36:28,840
Well, you don't have to apologise to me.

480
00:36:28,840 --> 00:36:31,720
You don't know how much l appreciate all this.

481
00:36:31,720 --> 00:36:34,430
What makes you so disgustingly cheerful this morning?

482
00:36:34,430 --> 00:36:36,640
Must be the spring.

483
00:36:36,640 --> 00:36:39,480
l thought maybe "believe you me" told you some more snappy stories.

484
00:36:39,480 --> 00:36:41,730
Oh no. He apologised for last night.

485
00:36:41,730 --> 00:36:44,170
Said he didn't know we were married.

486
00:36:44,170 --> 00:36:46,250
Just shows you how wrong a guy can be.

487
00:36:49,550 --> 00:36:51,680
-Donut?  -Thanks.

488
00:36:53,450 --> 00:36:55,590
You think this whole business is silly? Don't you?

489
00:36:55,590 --> 00:36:57,320
I mean running away and everything.

490
00:36:57,320 --> 00:36:58,490
No. Makes too good a story.

491
00:36:59,240 --> 00:37:02,590
Yes, you do. You think l'm a fool and a spoiled brat.

492
00:37:03,010 --> 00:37:05,340
Perhaps l am. Although, l don't see how l can be.

493
00:37:05,340 --> 00:37:07,680
Spoiled people are used to having their way.

494
00:37:07,680 --> 00:37:09,140
l never have. On the contrary.

495
00:37:09,140 --> 00:37:13,760
l've always been told what to do and how to do it and when and with whom.

496
00:37:14,740 --> 00:37:18,620
Would you believe, this is the first time l've ever been alone with a man?

497
00:37:18,620 --> 00:37:19,470
Yeah.

498
00:37:19,470 --> 00:37:21,330
lt's a wonder l'm not panic-stricken.

499
00:37:21,990 --> 00:37:23,170
You're doing all right.

500
00:37:24,060 --> 00:37:24,990
Thanks.

501
00:37:26,700 --> 00:37:30,130
Nurses, governesses, chaperones,

502
00:37:30,130 --> 00:37:32,820
even bodyguards. lt's been a lot of fun.

503
00:37:32,890 --> 00:37:35,260
One consolation, you can never get lonesome.

504
00:37:36,290 --> 00:37:38,630
lt has its moments. lt's become a sort of game,

505
00:37:38,630 --> 00:37:39,930
trying to outwit father's detectives.

506
00:37:41,050 --> 00:37:45,930
l did once. Actually went shopping without a bodyguard.

507
00:37:45,930 --> 00:37:47,590
lt was swell. l felt absolutely immoral.

508
00:37:47,590 --> 00:37:50,410
lt didn't last long, they found me in a department store.

509
00:37:50,410 --> 00:37:55,210
l was so mad, l ran out the back way and jumped into the first car l saw.

510
00:37:55,210 --> 00:37:55,930
Guess who was in it?

511
00:37:56,060 --> 00:37:58,690
Santa Claus?

512
00:37:58,690 --> 00:37:59,350
Ghandi?

513
00:37:59,350 --> 00:38:01,360
King Westley was in it.

514
00:38:02,820 --> 00:38:05,260
-ls that how you met him?  -Em.

515
00:38:05,260 --> 00:38:08,390
We rode around all afternoon. Father was frantic.

516
00:38:08,390 --> 00:38:10,710
By 6:00, he was having all the rivers dragged.

517
00:38:13,320 --> 00:38:15,590
Where'd you learn to dunk, in finishing school?

518
00:38:16,890 --> 00:38:19,380
Oh! Now don't you start telling me l shouldn't dunk.

519
00:38:19,380 --> 00:38:20,650
Of course you shouldn't. You don't know how to do it.

520
00:38:20,650 --> 00:38:24,440
Dunking is an art. Don't let it soak so long.

521
00:38:24,450 --> 00:38:26,130
A dip and sock, into your mouth.

522
00:38:26,130 --> 00:38:28,610
You leave it in too long, it gets soft and falls off.

523
00:38:28,610 --> 00:38:31,680
lt's all a matter of timing. l'll write a book about it.

524
00:38:32,430 --> 00:38:33,650
Thanks, professor.

525
00:38:33,650 --> 00:38:37,270
Just goes to show you. $20 million, and you don't know how to dunk.

526
00:38:37,810 --> 00:38:40,310
l'd change places with a plumber's daughter any day.

527
00:38:42,200 --> 00:38:44,570
How do l know who you are? l never saw you before.

528
00:38:44,570 --> 00:38:47,470
You can't go around bothering my tenants.

529
00:38:47,470 --> 00:38:49,160
There's no girl by that name here.

530
00:38:49,630 --> 00:38:51,270
How do l know you're detectives?

531
00:38:51,270 --> 00:38:53,220
Show him your credentials, Mac.

532
00:38:56,210 --> 00:38:57,490
Detectives.

533
00:38:58,410 --> 00:39:01,270
That's father at work. Peter, what'll l do?

534
00:39:01,270 --> 00:39:03,350
What'll l do?Maybe l can jump out of the window.

535
00:39:03,350 --> 00:39:04,200
They won't see me.

536
00:39:04,200 --> 00:39:06,240
Sit down. Get yourself all mussed up.

537
00:39:06,240 --> 00:39:09,190
Get your hair down over your eyes and undo your buttons.

538
00:39:11,250 --> 00:39:12,960
l got a letter from Aunt Bella last week.

539
00:39:12,960 --> 00:39:16,190
She said if we don't stop over in Wilkes-Barre, she'll never forgive us.

540
00:39:16,190 --> 00:39:18,390
What are you talking about?

541
00:39:18,390 --> 00:39:21,160
The baby's due next month. They want us to come.

542
00:39:22,800 --> 00:39:25,070
Oh, yeah yeah, She saw your sister on the street the other day.

543
00:39:25,070 --> 00:39:26,120
Said she's looking swell.

544
00:39:29,260 --> 00:39:30,430
Come in.

545
00:39:30,430 --> 00:39:33,110
You don't know, l hope Aunt Bella has a boy, don't you?

546
00:39:33,110 --> 00:39:36,070
Grandma says it's gonna be a girl. She hasn't missed calling one in years.

547
00:39:38,150 --> 00:39:40,170
Man here to see you, sweetheart.

548
00:39:40,170 --> 00:39:41,750
Who, me? You wanna see me?

549
00:39:41,750 --> 00:39:43,750
What's your name?

550
00:39:43,750 --> 00:39:46,970
-Are you addressing me?  -Yeah. What's your name?

551
00:39:46,970 --> 00:39:50,430
Hey! Wait a minute. That's my wife you're talking to.

552
00:39:50,430 --> 00:39:52,900
What do you mean coming here? What do you want anyway?

553
00:39:52,900 --> 00:39:56,070
-We're looking for somebody.  -Fine, but don't come busting in here.

554
00:39:56,070 --> 00:39:57,630
This isn't a public park.

555
00:39:57,630 --> 00:39:58,900
l got news to take a sock at you.

556
00:39:58,900 --> 00:40:02,090
-Take it easy, son. Take it easy.  -The men are detectives.

557
00:40:02,090 --> 00:40:03,780
I donn't care Even if they're the whole police department...

558
00:40:03,780 --> 00:40:06,010
...they can't bust in here, questioning my wife.

559
00:40:06,010 --> 00:40:09,120
Don't get so excited. He asked you a simple question.

560
00:40:10,170 --> 00:40:12,240
ls that so? How many times have l told you

561
00:40:12,240 --> 00:40:13,510
not to butt in when I have an argument?

562
00:40:13,510 --> 00:40:15,300
You don't have to lose your temper!

563
00:40:15,300 --> 00:40:19,540
As usual. Every time l try to protect you.

564
00:40:19,540 --> 00:40:22,460
At the elks dance, when that big Swede hit on you.

565
00:40:22,460 --> 00:40:25,140
He did not! l told you a million times.

566
00:40:25,140 --> 00:40:27,730
No, I saw him. He kept pawing you all over the dance floor.

567
00:40:27,730 --> 00:40:29,360
He didn't. You were drunk.

568
00:40:29,360 --> 00:40:31,730
Nuts! Just like your old man.

569
00:40:31,730 --> 00:40:33,870
Once a plumber's daughter, always a plumber's daughter.

570
00:40:33,870 --> 00:40:35,950
There ain't an ounce of brains in your family.

571
00:40:35,950 --> 00:40:38,230
Oh, Peter Warne, you've gone far enough!

572
00:40:38,230 --> 00:40:41,180
-Shut up!  -You see what you've done?

573
00:40:41,180 --> 00:40:45,070
Sorry, Mr Warne, but you see, we've gotta check up on everybody.

574
00:40:45,070 --> 00:40:47,550
We're looking for a girl named Ellen Andrews.

575
00:40:47,550 --> 00:40:49,870
You know, daughter of that big Wall Street mogul.

576
00:40:49,870 --> 00:40:51,950
Too bad you're not looking for a plumber's daughter.

577
00:40:51,950 --> 00:40:54,570
Quit bawling!

578
00:40:54,570 --> 00:40:58,060
l told you they were a perfectly nice married couple.

579
00:41:11,610 --> 00:41:13,280
You weren't bad, jumping in like that.

580
00:41:13,280 --> 00:41:16,360
-You've got a brain.  -You're not so bad, yourself.

581
00:41:16,360 --> 00:41:18,060
You know we could start a two-people stock company.

582
00:41:18,060 --> 00:41:20,290
Things get tough, we'll play to small town auditoriums.

583
00:41:20,730 --> 00:41:22,470
We'll call this one, "The Great Deception."

584
00:41:23,040 --> 00:41:25,570
What about "Cinderella" or a real hot love story?

585
00:41:25,570 --> 00:41:26,880
No, no, too mushy.

586
00:41:26,940 --> 00:41:28,320
l like mushy stuff.

587
00:41:29,730 --> 00:41:31,900
Quit bawling! Quit bawling!

588
00:41:32,330 --> 00:41:33,530
Bus leaves in five minutes!

589
00:41:33,530 --> 00:41:35,630
-What?  -Your bus leaves in five minutes.

590
00:41:35,960 --> 00:41:39,320
Oh! Holy smoke, we're not even packed yet.

591
00:41:43,290 --> 00:41:45,620
l'm starting not to believe you couldn't find your way home.

592
00:41:45,690 --> 00:41:47,150
This is the last session I want....

593
00:41:47,480 --> 00:41:49,890
-Yeah?  -Telegram for you.

594
00:41:49,890 --> 00:41:52,270
-Bring it in.  -Another wire from Peter Warne.

595
00:41:52,270 --> 00:41:56,650
Warne? Throw it in the wastebasket. Wait a minute. What does it say?

596
00:41:58,180 --> 00:42:01,720
"Have l got a story. Stop. lt's getting hotter and hotter. Stop.

597
00:42:01,720 --> 00:42:03,220
"Hope you're the same."

598
00:42:05,770 --> 00:42:06,920
-Collect?  -Yes.

599
00:42:06,920 --> 00:42:09,070
-lf you accept another one, you're fired.

600
00:42:09,070 --> 00:42:09,650
-Yes, sir.

601
00:42:09,650 --> 00:42:11,780
And that gives me a good idea for all of you.

602
00:42:12,530 --> 00:42:14,320
l want action, Lovington, action.

603
00:42:14,320 --> 00:42:16,060
We can't do the impossible, Mr. Andrews.

604
00:42:16,060 --> 00:42:17,790
What I'm asking isn't impossible.

605
00:42:17,790 --> 00:42:19,560
My daughter's somewhere between here and Miami.

606
00:42:19,560 --> 00:42:20,440
Now l want her found.

607
00:42:20,440 --> 00:42:23,000
-l put extra men on, the whole way.  -That's not enough.

608
00:42:23,460 --> 00:42:24,670
Send in Clark and Brown.

609
00:42:24,670 --> 00:42:27,410
-You sure she isn't with King Westley?  -No.

610
00:42:27,410 --> 00:42:30,260
He's being trailed 24 hours a day since this thing started.

611
00:42:30,260 --> 00:42:32,730
He can't even get a phone call we don't know about.

612
00:42:32,730 --> 00:42:36,120
l'm worried, Lovington. After all, something might have happened to her.

613
00:42:36,120 --> 00:42:36,570
l don't think so.

614
00:42:36,570 --> 00:42:40,370
Brown, I want you to make an arrangement for a radio broadcast right away.

615
00:42:40,370 --> 00:42:41,550
Coast-to-coast hook up. Offer a reward of...

616
00:42:41,550 --> 00:42:44,250
...$10,000 for information on her whereabouts.

617
00:42:44,250 --> 00:42:44,760
Yes, sir.

618
00:42:44,760 --> 00:42:47,370
Clark, send the story to all of the newspapers.

619
00:42:47,370 --> 00:42:49,890
Some out-of-town papers may not have a picture of her.

620
00:42:49,890 --> 00:42:53,510
Here. Wire this to them. l want the story to break right away.

621
00:42:53,510 --> 00:42:54,150
Yes, sir.

622
00:42:54,150 --> 00:42:56,110
Now we'll get some action!

623
00:43:31,540 --> 00:43:33,400
Fine, that's fine.

624
00:43:35,330 --> 00:43:38,740
You know that one about the man who flew on the trapeze?

625
00:43:38,740 --> 00:43:39,600
Yeah.

626
00:43:45,920 --> 00:43:50,020
"Once l was happy but now l'm forlorn

627
00:43:50,020 --> 00:43:54,180
"Like an old coat that is tattered and torn

628
00:43:54,180 --> 00:43:58,310
"Left in this wide world to weep and to mourn

629
00:43:58,310 --> 00:44:01,790
"Betrayed by a maid in her teens

630
00:44:02,210 --> 00:44:05,240
"This maid that l loved she was handsome

631
00:44:06,240 --> 00:44:09,810
"And l tried all l knew how to please

632
00:44:10,220 --> 00:44:14,120
"But l never could please her one-quarter so well

633
00:44:14,120 --> 00:44:18,060
"As the man on the flying trapeze

634
00:44:18,060 --> 00:44:21,900
"He flies through the air with the greatest of ease

635
00:44:21,900 --> 00:44:25,950
"The daring young man on the flying trapeze

636
00:44:25,950 --> 00:44:29,780
"His actions are graceful, all the girls he does please

637
00:44:29,780 --> 00:44:33,310
"And my love he has stolen away"

638
00:44:40,250 --> 00:44:42,480
l know the second verse there.

639
00:44:44,510 --> 00:44:48,420
"Now he'd play with a miss like a cat with a mouse

640
00:44:48,420 --> 00:44:52,140
"His eyes would undress every girl in the house

641
00:44:52,140 --> 00:44:57,200
"Perhaps he is better described as a louse

642
00:44:57,200 --> 00:44:59,900
And still people came just the same

643
00:44:59,900 --> 00:45:03,960
"Now he smiles from the bar on the people below

644
00:45:03,960 --> 00:45:07,270
"And one night he smiled on my love

645
00:45:08,090 --> 00:45:10,020
"She blew him a kiss

646
00:45:10,020 --> 00:45:15,830
"And she hollered bravo And he hung by his schnozzle from above

647
00:45:15,830 --> 00:45:20,190
"He floats through the air with the greatest of ease

648
00:45:20,190 --> 00:45:26,100
"Daring young man on the flying trapeze His actions are graceful

649
00:45:26,100 --> 00:45:31,360
"All the girls he does please And my love he has stolen away"

650
00:45:34,660 --> 00:45:36,690
Do you mind if l take the third one?

651
00:45:41,770 --> 00:45:45,620
"l wept and l whimpered l simpered for weeks

652
00:45:45,620 --> 00:45:49,380
"While she spent her time with the circus' freaks

653
00:45:49,380 --> 00:45:53,310
"The tears were like hailstones that rolled down my cheeks

654
00:45:53,310 --> 00:45:56,700
"Alas, Alack and Alaska

655
00:45:57,210 --> 00:46:00,540
"l went to this fellow the villain, and l said

656
00:46:00,540 --> 00:46:03,890
"l'll see that you get your deserts

657
00:46:04,340 --> 00:46:07,840
"His thumb to his nose he put up with a sneer

658
00:46:07,840 --> 00:46:10,150
"He sneered once again and said

659
00:46:11,920 --> 00:46:15,560
"He flies through the air with the greatest of ease

660
00:46:15,560 --> 00:46:19,330
"That daring young man on the flying trapeze

661
00:46:19,330 --> 00:46:23,050
"His actions are graceful The girls he does please

662
00:46:23,050 --> 00:46:26,600
"My love he has stolen away"

663
00:46:34,540 --> 00:46:37,600
-Everybody keep your seats.  -Thank the man for me, Peter.

664
00:46:37,600 --> 00:46:40,330
lt's the first comfortable position l've been in all night.

665
00:46:41,870 --> 00:46:45,270
"She flies through the air with the greatest of ease

666
00:46:45,270 --> 00:46:46,200
"The daring young--"

667
00:46:46,200 --> 00:46:51,050
Mon, mon, What's the matter with you? Help! Somebody help.

668
00:46:51,050 --> 00:46:52,360
Something happened to her.

669
00:46:52,360 --> 00:46:53,810
Look how pale she is.

670
00:47:02,860 --> 00:47:04,650
Let's give her a chance to snap out of it.

671
00:47:06,890 --> 00:47:09,090
Don't worry. She'll be all right.

672
00:47:09,950 --> 00:47:12,690
We ain't ate nothing since yesterday.

673
00:47:14,390 --> 00:47:16,470
What happened to your money?

674
00:47:16,470 --> 00:47:20,950
Ma spent it all on the tickets. We didn't know it was gonna be so much.

675
00:47:21,820 --> 00:47:24,020
We shouldn't have come, l guess.

676
00:47:24,800 --> 00:47:27,910
But Ma said there was a job waiting for her in New York...

677
00:47:27,910 --> 00:47:30,660
...and if we didn't go, she might lose it.

678
00:47:36,280 --> 00:47:38,790
She'll be all right when she's had something to eat.

679
00:47:40,150 --> 00:47:42,820
Here honey, the next time we come to, you buy some food. Now come on.

680
00:47:42,820 --> 00:47:47,070
l shouldn't ought to take this. Ma'll get mad.

681
00:47:47,070 --> 00:47:50,000
Just don't tell her about it. You don't want her to get sick again.

682
00:47:50,000 --> 00:47:51,950
No, but you might need it.

683
00:47:51,950 --> 00:47:53,070
Come on.

684
00:47:53,070 --> 00:47:54,010
l got millions.

685
00:47:54,010 --> 00:47:55,080
Here.

686
00:47:55,080 --> 00:47:56,760
-Thanks.  -Come on, go back.

687
00:48:15,210 --> 00:48:16,800
Better phone for some help.

688
00:48:16,880 --> 00:48:19,630
Hey go phone if you want to. The nearest town is 10 miles away here.

689
00:48:19,630 --> 00:48:20,380
Yeah?

690
00:48:21,230 --> 00:48:24,900
Say, buddy. Like to take a look at my paper?

691
00:48:25,900 --> 00:48:29,000
Travelling like this, you kind lose track of what's going on in the world.

692
00:48:29,640 --> 00:48:32,390
Take that story there, for instance.

693
00:48:33,260 --> 00:48:35,590
lf l was to see that dame, you know what l'd do?

694
00:48:35,690 --> 00:48:36,800
No. What?

695
00:48:37,570 --> 00:48:39,180
l'd go fifty-fifty with you.

696
00:48:40,330 --> 00:48:40,960
Why?

697
00:48:41,040 --> 00:48:42,890
Because l don't believe in hogging.

698
00:48:42,960 --> 00:48:46,320
A bird that figures that way always ends up behind the eight ball.

699
00:48:46,320 --> 00:48:47,390
That's what l always say.

700
00:48:51,420 --> 00:48:52,240
What's on your mind?

701
00:48:53,460 --> 00:48:55,620
Five G's or l crab the works.

702
00:49:02,120 --> 00:49:04,610
Let's get away from here and talk this over privately.

703
00:49:04,610 --> 00:49:06,850
l knew she wasn't your wife all the time.

704
00:49:10,090 --> 00:49:14,750
Lucky thing, my running into you. Just the man l need.

705
00:49:14,750 --> 00:49:16,330
You made no mistake, believe me.

706
00:49:16,340 --> 00:49:17,620
l can use a smart guy like you.

707
00:49:17,620 --> 00:49:19,730
Say listen. When you're talking to old man Shapeley...

708
00:49:19,730 --> 00:49:20,960
Can you make a gat?

709
00:49:21,780 --> 00:49:22,440
Huh?

710
00:49:22,890 --> 00:49:24,970
A gat. A gat. A rod.

711
00:49:25,910 --> 00:49:27,640
-Got any fireworks on you?  -No.

712
00:49:29,150 --> 00:49:32,820
l got a couple of machine guns in my suitcase. l'll give you one of them.

713
00:49:32,820 --> 00:49:36,140
May have trouble up north. Have to shoot it out with the cops.

714
00:49:36,140 --> 00:49:39,730
lf you manage, those five G's are as good as in the bag. Maybe more.

715
00:49:39,730 --> 00:49:41,970
l'll talk to the Killer, he'll take care of you.

716
00:49:41,970 --> 00:49:43,220
Killer?

717
00:49:43,220 --> 00:49:45,540
Yeah. The big boy. The boss of the outfit.

718
00:49:46,610 --> 00:49:48,310
You're not kidnapping her, are you?

719
00:49:48,870 --> 00:49:49,610
What else, stupid?

720
00:49:49,620 --> 00:49:52,450
You don't think we're after that penny-ante reward?

721
00:49:52,450 --> 00:49:55,610
$10, 000? Chicken feed.

722
00:49:56,280 --> 00:49:59,170
Now listen, we're holding that dame for a million smackers.

723
00:49:59,170 --> 00:50:02,410
Say, l didn't know it was anything like this. You see, l've got....

724
00:50:03,630 --> 00:50:05,890
What's the matter? You getting yellow?

725
00:50:05,890 --> 00:50:08,790
l'm a married man. l got a couple of kids. l can't afford to get....

726
00:50:08,790 --> 00:50:11,730
Hu...Pipe down your mug before l....

727
00:50:12,870 --> 00:50:14,790
What are you trying to do, tell the whole world about it?

728
00:50:15,770 --> 00:50:18,620
And now listen, you're into this thing and you're staying in, get me?

729
00:50:18,620 --> 00:50:19,650
You know too much.

730
00:50:20,290 --> 00:50:22,650
l won't, I won't say anything, honest l won't.

731
00:50:22,650 --> 00:50:25,430
How do l know that? l got a notion to plug you.

732
00:50:25,430 --> 00:50:27,210
Why should l take a chance with you?

733
00:50:27,210 --> 00:50:29,700
Trust me, mister. l'll keep my mouth shut.

734
00:50:29,700 --> 00:50:31,080
Yeah?

735
00:50:33,000 --> 00:50:34,180
What's your name?

736
00:50:34,180 --> 00:50:36,130
Oscar Shapeley.

737
00:50:36,130 --> 00:50:38,520
-Where do you live?  -Orange, New Jersey.

738
00:50:39,120 --> 00:50:41,140
Got a couple of kids?

739
00:50:41,140 --> 00:50:44,600
Yes, sir. Just babies. A little golden-haired girl.

740
00:50:44,600 --> 00:50:46,760
-You love them, don't you?  -Yes, yes, l do.

741
00:50:47,740 --> 00:50:49,350
You wouldn't. You're not thinking of--

742
00:50:49,350 --> 00:50:52,090
-You keep your trap shut, all right?  -Sure. Sure. Sure

743
00:50:52,090 --> 00:50:54,710
-lf you don't....  -l'll keep my trap shut. l will. l will. l will.

744
00:50:54,710 --> 00:50:56,220
You ever hear of Bugs Dooley?

745
00:50:57,260 --> 00:50:58,930
Bugs Dooley? No.

746
00:50:58,930 --> 00:51:02,450
He was a nice guy, just like you. And he made a big mistake one day.

747
00:51:02,450 --> 00:51:04,260
Got a little too talkative.

748
00:51:04,260 --> 00:51:05,980
-You know what happened to his kid?  -No.

749
00:51:05,980 --> 00:51:09,020
l can't tell you. But when Bugs heard about it he blew his brains out.

750
00:51:09,280 --> 00:51:10,550
Oh, that's...that's terrible.

751
00:51:10,550 --> 00:51:15,110
He had it coming to him. He talked too much. l never talk.

752
00:51:15,110 --> 00:51:17,620
l never say a word. Word...word of honour.

753
00:51:17,620 --> 00:51:20,390
l wouldn't want anything to happen to my kids.

754
00:51:20,390 --> 00:51:22,580
Okay. Just remember that.

755
00:51:24,010 --> 00:51:25,480
Now beat it.

756
00:51:25,480 --> 00:51:29,090
Sure, mister. Thanks. l always knew you guys were--

757
00:51:29,090 --> 00:51:32,600
Come on, scram. And stay away from that bus.

758
00:51:32,600 --> 00:51:34,520
Sure. Anything you say, mister.

759
00:51:35,580 --> 00:51:37,720
-You wouldn't shoot me in the back?  -lf you don't beat it....

760
00:51:37,720 --> 00:51:38,870
l'm going.

761
00:51:54,860 --> 00:51:56,810
What's the matter? Why do we have to leave the bus?

762
00:51:56,910 --> 00:51:58,770
Come on. Don't ask so many questions.

763
00:51:58,830 --> 00:52:00,080
Why?

764
00:52:06,640 --> 00:52:09,570
Poor old Shapeley. You shouldn't have frightened him like that.

765
00:52:09,710 --> 00:52:13,190
At the rate he's going, he's probably crossed two state lines by this time.

766
00:52:13,970 --> 00:52:16,750
Why did we have to leave the bus?

767
00:52:17,010 --> 00:52:20,110
When Shapeley stops running, he's going to start thinking, isn't he?

768
00:52:20,950 --> 00:52:24,430
You know l've been doing a little thinking myself.

769
00:52:24,980 --> 00:52:27,500
The next town we come to, you better wire your father.

770
00:52:28,850 --> 00:52:30,740
What's the matter, are you weakening?

771
00:52:30,840 --> 00:52:35,470
No. l was just thinking of you. A starvation diet may not agree with you.

772
00:52:35,730 --> 00:52:37,770
Did you give that child all your money?

773
00:52:37,880 --> 00:52:40,430
l gave him nothing. You were the big-hearted gal.

774
00:52:41,070 --> 00:52:43,340
All the money l had was that ten spot.

775
00:52:43,430 --> 00:52:46,370
So l've been thinking you better wire your father.

776
00:52:46,540 --> 00:52:50,610
No, sir. l started out for New York and l'm going to get there...

777
00:52:50,610 --> 00:52:53,060
...if l have to starve all the way.

778
00:52:53,260 --> 00:52:54,090
Okay.

779
00:52:55,050 --> 00:52:58,630
What is this strange power this man Westley has over you women?

780
00:52:58,700 --> 00:53:00,640
Here, take these.

781
00:53:01,340 --> 00:53:04,080
-Hold on to them. Get up on that log.  -That?

782
00:53:04,080 --> 00:53:05,480
Get up on the log.

783
00:53:16,990 --> 00:53:18,580
l wish you'd stop being playful.

784
00:53:18,650 --> 00:53:20,290
Oh, so sorry, sorry.

785
00:53:20,290 --> 00:53:24,240
You know, this is the first time in years l've ridden piggyback.

786
00:53:24,410 --> 00:53:25,620
This isn't piggyback.

787
00:53:25,720 --> 00:53:27,900
-Of course it is.  -You're crazy.

788
00:53:28,600 --> 00:53:32,250
l remember distinctly my father taking me for a piggyback ride.

789
00:53:32,350 --> 00:53:34,010
-And he carried you like this?  -Yes.

790
00:53:34,140 --> 00:53:36,790
Your father didn't know beans about piggyback riding.

791
00:53:37,530 --> 00:53:39,860
My uncle, mother's brother, has four children.

792
00:53:39,860 --> 00:53:41,500
l've seen them ride piggyback.

793
00:53:41,560 --> 00:53:43,610
l'll bet there isn't a good piggyback rider in your family.

794
00:53:43,610 --> 00:53:46,040
l never knew a rich man who could piggyback ride.

795
00:53:48,030 --> 00:53:49,880
You're prejudiced.

796
00:53:50,750 --> 00:53:54,140
You show me a good piggy backer. l'll show you a real human.

797
00:53:54,140 --> 00:53:57,480
Take Abraham Lincoln for instance. A natural born piggy backer.

798
00:53:57,480 --> 00:54:00,330
Where do you get off with that stuffed-shirt family of yours?

799
00:54:02,880 --> 00:54:05,690
My father was a great piggy backer.

800
00:54:06,910 --> 00:54:08,340
Here, hold this a minute.

801
00:54:12,630 --> 00:54:13,430
Thank you.

802
00:54:19,180 --> 00:54:22,490
How long does this keep up? My feet are killing me.

803
00:54:35,760 --> 00:54:37,410
This looks like the best spot.

804
00:54:38,910 --> 00:54:41,110
We're not going to sleep out here, are we?

805
00:54:41,530 --> 00:54:44,670
l don't know about you, but l'm going to give a good imitation of it.

806
00:54:45,330 --> 00:54:46,080
Peter?

807
00:54:46,650 --> 00:54:47,790
What?

808
00:54:48,430 --> 00:54:50,000
l'm awfully hungry.

809
00:54:50,880 --> 00:54:52,150
lt's just your imagination.

810
00:54:52,150 --> 00:54:53,180
No, it isn't.

811
00:54:53,870 --> 00:54:56,600
l'm hungry and scared.

812
00:54:57,120 --> 00:54:59,690
You can't be hungry and scared both at the same time.

813
00:54:59,690 --> 00:55:00,760
Well, l am.

814
00:55:00,760 --> 00:55:02,860
lf you're scared, it scares the hunger out of you.

815
00:55:03,500 --> 00:55:05,450
Not if you're more hungry than scared.

816
00:55:06,280 --> 00:55:09,420
All right, you win. Let's forget about it.

817
00:55:11,550 --> 00:55:13,530
l can't forget it. l'm still hungry.

818
00:55:14,630 --> 00:55:18,860
Holy smoke! Why did l ever get mixed up with you?

819
00:55:19,590 --> 00:55:22,210
lf l had any sense, l'd be in New York by this time.

820
00:55:22,700 --> 00:55:24,220
What about your story?

821
00:55:24,300 --> 00:55:26,850
Taking a married woman back to her husband.

822
00:55:30,440 --> 00:55:32,680
l turned out to be the prize sucker.

823
00:55:34,670 --> 00:55:37,290
All right, come on. Your bed's all ready.

824
00:55:39,150 --> 00:55:41,110
l'll get my clothes all wrinkled.

825
00:55:41,110 --> 00:55:42,760
-Then take them off.  -What?

826
00:55:42,760 --> 00:55:46,730
All right, don't take them off. Do what you please, but shut up about it.

827
00:56:17,820 --> 00:56:19,940
You know you're becoming awfully disagreeable lately.

828
00:56:20,900 --> 00:56:24,200
You just snap my head off every time l open my mouth.

829
00:56:26,980 --> 00:56:30,370
lf being with me is so distasteful to you, you can leave.

830
00:56:32,170 --> 00:56:35,170
You can leave any time you see fit.

831
00:56:35,400 --> 00:56:37,700
Nobody's holding you here.

832
00:56:38,760 --> 00:56:41,440
l can get along.

833
00:56:46,840 --> 00:56:48,830
Peter?

834
00:56:50,750 --> 00:56:51,890
Peter!

835
00:56:53,840 --> 00:57:00,750
Oh! Peter! Peter! Peter! Peter!

836
00:57:00,750 --> 00:57:03,420
-What's the matter?  -l was so scared!

837
00:57:04,730 --> 00:57:06,980
What's got into you? l left for a minute to find you something to eat.

838
00:57:06,980 --> 00:57:08,310
Oh, l know but....

839
00:57:08,310 --> 00:57:09,950
Here, eat your head off.

840
00:57:10,510 --> 00:57:11,980
l don't want it now.

841
00:57:11,980 --> 00:57:14,600
-l thought you said you were hungry.  -l was, but--

842
00:57:14,600 --> 00:57:15,170
But what?

843
00:57:17,070 --> 00:57:19,020
l was so scared, it scared the hunger--

844
00:57:19,020 --> 00:57:22,150
Holy jumping catfish. You drive a guy crazy.

845
00:58:05,560 --> 00:58:06,940
lt's liable to get chilly before morning.

846
00:58:06,940 --> 00:58:08,310
Better use this.

847
00:58:45,570 --> 00:58:47,790
What are you thinking about?

848
00:58:48,900 --> 00:58:51,350
By a strange coincidence, l was thinking of you.

849
00:58:52,710 --> 00:58:54,210
-Really?  -Yeah.

850
00:58:56,390 --> 00:58:59,250
l was just wondering what makes dames like you so dizzy.

851
00:59:34,120 --> 00:59:36,330
What did you say we're supposed to be doing?

852
00:59:36,430 --> 00:59:37,670
Hitchhiking.

853
00:59:39,920 --> 00:59:43,490
Well, you've given me a very good example of the hiking.

854
00:59:44,120 --> 00:59:45,750
Where does the hitching come in?

855
00:59:45,750 --> 00:59:48,410
lt's a little early yet. No cars out.

856
00:59:51,160 --> 00:59:53,060
lf it's the same to you...

857
00:59:54,010 --> 00:59:56,780
...l'm going to sit right here and wait until they come.

858
01:00:08,300 --> 01:00:09,710
You got a toothpick?

859
01:00:09,710 --> 01:00:12,520
-What's the matter?  -l got hay in my teeth.

860
01:00:12,520 --> 01:00:15,500
No, l haven't got a toothpick. Here, l got a penknife, though.

861
01:00:16,690 --> 01:00:17,860
Now hold still.

862
01:00:17,860 --> 01:00:20,170
-Be careful.  -All right. Where is it?

863
01:00:22,310 --> 01:00:22,880
All right, now hold still.

864
01:00:23,850 --> 01:00:26,970
Here. Get it?

865
01:00:27,630 --> 01:00:28,810
Thanks.

866
01:00:29,580 --> 01:00:31,370
Hey, you should have swallowed that.

867
01:00:31,370 --> 01:00:32,120
You won't have any breakfast, you know?

868
01:00:32,820 --> 01:00:34,270
You needn't rub it in.

869
01:00:38,910 --> 01:00:41,100
-What are you eating?  -Carrots.

870
01:00:41,640 --> 01:00:43,740
-Raw?  -Want one?

871
01:00:43,740 --> 01:00:48,510
No. Why didn't you get me something l could eat?

872
01:00:48,510 --> 01:00:52,310
That's right, l forgot. The idea of offering a raw carrot to an Andrews.

873
01:00:53,150 --> 01:00:55,300
You don't think l'm going around panhandling for you, do you?

874
01:00:56,070 --> 01:00:58,150
Have one of these. Best thing for you, carrots.

875
01:00:58,150 --> 01:01:00,560
l hate the horrid things.

876
01:01:03,100 --> 01:01:05,670
l wish you wouldn't talk so much. Now we let a car get away.

877
01:01:06,520 --> 01:01:08,720
And suppose nobody stops for us?

878
01:01:09,200 --> 01:01:12,250
They'll stop all right. lt's a matter of knowing how to handle them.

879
01:01:12,970 --> 01:01:14,630
And you're an expert l suppose.

880
01:01:14,630 --> 01:01:18,300
Expert. And l'll write a book about it. Call it "The Hitchhiker's Hail."

881
01:01:18,300 --> 01:01:21,340
There's no end to your accomplishments, is there?

882
01:01:21,830 --> 01:01:23,530
-You think it's simple?  -No.

883
01:01:24,230 --> 01:01:26,500
Well, it is simple. lt's all in that old thumb, see?

884
01:01:27,160 --> 01:01:30,180
Some people do it like this. Or like this.

885
01:01:31,670 --> 01:01:33,350
All wrong. Never get anywhere.

886
01:01:33,350 --> 01:01:34,520
Oh, the poor things.

887
01:01:34,520 --> 01:01:38,530
But that old thumb never fails. lt's all a matter of how you do it, though.

888
01:01:38,720 --> 01:01:41,320
You know, now you take No. 1, for instance.

889
01:01:41,320 --> 01:01:44,820
That's a short jerky movement, like this. That shows independence.

890
01:01:44,820 --> 01:01:46,440
You don't care if they stop or not. You got money.

891
01:01:47,510 --> 01:01:50,600
-Clever.  -Yeak, but No. 2, that's a little wider movement.

892
01:01:50,600 --> 01:01:54,020
Smile goes with this one, like this.

893
01:01:54,850 --> 01:01:57,350
That means you got a brand-new story about the farmer's daughter.

894
01:01:59,690 --> 01:02:01,800
You figured that out all by yourself?.

895
01:02:01,800 --> 01:02:05,600
That's nothing. No. 3, that's a pip. That's the pitiful one.

896
01:02:05,600 --> 01:02:08,950
You know when you're broke and hungry, everything looks black.

897
01:02:08,950 --> 01:02:12,370
lt's a long sweeping movement like this. Gotta follow through, though.

898
01:02:13,960 --> 01:02:14,960
Oh, that's amazing.

899
01:02:14,960 --> 01:02:17,620
Yeah! But it's no good, if you haven't got a long face to go with it.

900
01:02:18,470 --> 01:02:20,040
Here comes a car.

901
01:02:20,040 --> 01:02:23,310
Okay. Now watch me. l'm gonna use No. 1.

902
01:02:23,310 --> 01:02:24,940
Keep your eye on that thumb, baby, and see what happens.

903
01:02:31,610 --> 01:02:33,450
l still got my eye on the thumb.

904
01:02:34,010 --> 01:02:36,950
Something must have gone wrong. l'll try No. 2.

905
01:02:37,580 --> 01:02:40,200
When you get to 100, wake me up.

906
01:03:20,450 --> 01:03:23,350
l don't think l'll write that book after all.

907
01:03:23,520 --> 01:03:25,530
Think of all the fun you had, though.

908
01:03:27,290 --> 01:03:28,950
You mind if l try?

909
01:03:29,890 --> 01:03:31,430
You?

910
01:03:31,430 --> 01:03:34,010
Don't make me laugh.

911
01:03:34,970 --> 01:03:38,650
You're such a smart aleck. Nobody knows anything but you.

912
01:03:39,170 --> 01:03:41,920
l'll stop a car and l won't use my thumb.

913
01:03:42,620 --> 01:03:43,870
What are you gonna do?

914
01:03:44,350 --> 01:03:46,590
lt's a system all my own.

915
01:04:07,520 --> 01:04:09,430
Aren't you going to give me a little credit?

916
01:04:10,240 --> 01:04:11,580
What for?

917
01:04:11,930 --> 01:04:16,570
Well, l proved once and for all that the limb is mightier than the thumb.

918
01:04:17,210 --> 01:04:20,410
Why didn't you take off all your clothes? You could have stopped 40 cars.

919
01:04:20,480 --> 01:04:23,630
l'll remember that when we need 40 cars.

920
01:04:24,370 --> 01:04:28,220
So, you're just married? That's pretty good.

921
01:04:28,220 --> 01:04:33,910
But if l was young, that's the way l'd spend my honeymoon. Hitchhiking.

922
01:04:34,400 --> 01:04:37,880
Yes, sir. "Hitchhiking down the highway

923
01:04:37,880 --> 01:04:42,130
"Of love on a honeymoon

924
01:04:42,130 --> 01:04:52,740
"Hitchhiking down...down...down...down the highway."

925
01:04:55,810 --> 01:04:59,570
Hey, hey! Aren't you afraid you'll burn out a tonsil?

926
01:04:59,570 --> 01:05:01,650
Tonsil? Me? No.

927
01:05:02,670 --> 01:05:05,270
Me burn a tonsil?

928
01:05:05,280 --> 01:05:08,350
"My tonsils won't burn, as likes..."

929
01:05:08,350 --> 01:05:11,190
All right, all right, let it go, let it go.

930
01:05:11,190 --> 01:05:12,790
"Turn"

931
01:05:22,110 --> 01:05:23,260
How about a bite to eat?

932
01:05:23,260 --> 01:05:25,790
-Well, I think that would be lovely.  -No thanks, we're not hungry.

933
01:05:25,790 --> 01:05:28,390
Oh, I see young people in love are never hungry.

934
01:05:28,390 --> 01:05:29,100
No.

935
01:05:29,100 --> 01:05:32,250
"Young people in love

936
01:05:32,250 --> 01:05:35,840
"Are very seldom hungry

937
01:05:35,840 --> 01:05:42,160
"People in love are very seldom hungry"

938
01:05:42,160 --> 01:05:45,550
What were you going to do? Gold dig that guy for a meal?

939
01:05:46,390 --> 01:05:48,920
Sure, l was. No fooling, l'm hungry.

940
01:05:49,430 --> 01:05:50,680
Eat a carrot.

941
01:05:51,700 --> 01:05:52,930
No.

942
01:05:54,100 --> 01:05:55,700
l'm going in to ask him.

943
01:05:55,700 --> 01:05:57,280
You do and l'll break your neck.

944
01:06:09,660 --> 01:06:11,820
Come on, let's get out of here. Stretch our legs.

945
01:06:38,940 --> 01:06:40,630
l'm sorry....

946
01:06:40,700 --> 01:06:42,360
Oh, that's all right.

947
01:06:52,910 --> 01:06:56,300
Hey! Hey! hey! Come here!

948
01:06:57,380 --> 01:06:59,280
Hey! You've got my suitcase!

949
01:07:22,020 --> 01:07:23,580
What happened to you? l was worried.

950
01:07:23,680 --> 01:07:26,720
-Get in.  -Look at your face! You've got a cut!

951
01:07:26,820 --> 01:07:27,800
Well, what happened?

952
01:07:27,940 --> 01:07:31,590
A road thief. Picks people up, runs off with their things. What a racket.

953
01:07:31,650 --> 01:07:32,900
How'd you get the car?

954
01:07:33,030 --> 01:07:36,000
l gave him a black eye for it and had to tie him up to a tree.

955
01:08:08,530 --> 01:08:10,840
Can't be much gas left in this thing.

956
01:08:10,840 --> 01:08:13,160
Gotta start promoting some.

957
01:08:15,090 --> 01:08:17,530
Better take the things out of the pocket of that coat.

958
01:08:18,670 --> 01:08:20,720
That'll be good for ten gallons.

959
01:08:56,810 --> 01:08:59,630
l haven't changed my mind, Westley. l want you to understand that.

960
01:08:59,630 --> 01:09:01,640
l don't like you. Never have.

961
01:09:01,640 --> 01:09:02,480
Never will.

962
01:09:02,480 --> 01:09:04,440
Now that's clear enough, isn't it?

963
01:09:04,440 --> 01:09:06,880
You've made it evident by your threats of annulment.

964
01:09:06,880 --> 01:09:09,400
Well, it hasn't worried me for a minute.

965
01:09:09,400 --> 01:09:11,190
Ellie and l got married because we love each other.

966
01:09:11,840 --> 01:09:13,400
She's proving it.

967
01:09:13,400 --> 01:09:15,530
As far as l'm concerned, there's going to be no annulment.

968
01:09:15,530 --> 01:09:21,240
l see. You've got hold of a good thing and you're going to hang on to it?

969
01:09:21,910 --> 01:09:26,690
All right, you win. I guess l'll just have to get used to you.

970
01:09:26,690 --> 01:09:30,910
l admit, l'm licked. But it's only because l'm worried.

971
01:09:31,610 --> 01:09:35,360
lf l don't find her soon, l'll go crazy.

972
01:09:35,360 --> 01:09:37,620
Mind l could have helped if it hadn't been for you.

973
01:09:37,620 --> 01:09:38,940
l've been watched so closely--

974
01:09:38,940 --> 01:09:43,270
Yes, I know, I know. Well, you can help now.

975
01:09:43,270 --> 01:09:45,050
l've got a room full of reporters in there.

976
01:09:45,050 --> 01:09:46,940
Now, l want you to make a statement.

977
01:09:46,940 --> 01:09:51,390
Say that we've talked things over and come to an understanding.

978
01:09:51,390 --> 01:09:55,490
And that if she returns l won't interfere with your marriage.

979
01:10:06,090 --> 01:10:08,520
-All right?  -Yeah, that's quite all right.

980
01:10:08,520 --> 01:10:09,400
Okay.

981
01:10:10,230 --> 01:10:12,590
l hope you and your wife spend a pleasant week with us.

982
01:10:12,590 --> 01:10:15,480
Yeah, yeah, so do l. Thank you. Goodnight.

983
01:10:15,480 --> 01:10:16,370
Goodnight.

984
01:10:18,980 --> 01:10:21,070
-All right, brat.  -Any luck?

985
01:10:21,070 --> 01:10:23,520
Yeah. He finally agreed to let us have a cabin.

986
01:10:23,690 --> 01:10:24,960
What about the money?

987
01:10:25,100 --> 01:10:28,500
l talked him out of that idea. He thinks we're staying a week.

988
01:10:28,500 --> 01:10:31,230
-l must think something up before morning.  -That's swell.

989
01:10:31,230 --> 01:10:36,750
Yeah? l'm glad you think so. lf you ask me, l think it's foolish.

990
01:10:36,750 --> 01:10:39,250
l told you there's no use in staying here.

991
01:10:39,250 --> 01:10:42,600
We can make New York in three hours.

992
01:10:45,530 --> 01:10:47,830
l thought you were in a hurry to get back.

993
01:10:53,330 --> 01:10:56,600
Well, whoever heard of getting in at 3:00 in the morning?

994
01:10:57,140 --> 01:10:59,170
Everybody will be asleep.

995
01:11:04,970 --> 01:11:08,110
Okay. Cottage no. 6.

996
01:11:33,680 --> 01:11:37,510
There you go, trusting people again. How many times did l tell you--

997
01:11:37,580 --> 01:11:41,230
But he looked like a nice, upright young fellow, Ma.

998
01:11:48,540 --> 01:11:49,940
We're on the last lap.

999
01:11:54,970 --> 01:11:57,210
Tomorrow morning, you'll be in the arms of your husband.

1000
01:11:57,210 --> 01:11:58,050
Yeah.

1001
01:12:00,840 --> 01:12:03,120
You'll have a great story, won't you?

1002
01:12:03,120 --> 01:12:05,950
Yeah. Swell.

1003
01:12:28,470 --> 01:12:29,790
Thanks.

1004
01:13:04,820 --> 01:13:07,150
We certainly outsmarted your father.

1005
01:13:08,730 --> 01:13:10,150
l guess you ought to be happy.

1006
01:13:11,260 --> 01:13:13,490
Am l going to see you in New York?

1007
01:13:15,830 --> 01:13:16,790
Nope.

1008
01:13:19,120 --> 01:13:20,400
Why not?

1009
01:13:21,750 --> 01:13:25,060
l don't make it a policy to run around with married women.

1010
01:13:27,200 --> 01:13:29,260
There's no harm in your coming to see us.

1011
01:13:31,290 --> 01:13:32,600
Not interested.

1012
01:13:36,320 --> 01:13:37,910
Won't l ever see you again?

1013
01:13:39,400 --> 01:13:41,530
What do you want to see me? l've served my purpose!

1014
01:13:41,530 --> 01:13:43,580
l brought you back to King Westley, didn't I?

1015
01:13:43,580 --> 01:13:44,400
That's what you wanted, wasn't it?

1016
01:14:21,540 --> 01:14:24,030
Have you ever been in love, Peter?

1017
01:14:25,190 --> 01:14:26,750
Me?

1018
01:14:27,650 --> 01:14:29,110
Yes.

1019
01:14:30,600 --> 01:14:33,250
Haven't you ever thought about it at all?

1020
01:14:36,090 --> 01:14:40,120
lt seems to me you could make some girl wonderfully happy.

1021
01:14:42,050 --> 01:14:44,960
Sure, l've thought about it. Who hasn't?

1022
01:14:48,800 --> 01:14:50,560
lf l could ever meet the right sort of girl.

1023
01:14:53,120 --> 01:14:54,440
Yeah, where are you gonna find her?

1024
01:14:54,440 --> 01:14:57,070
Somebody that's real. Somebody that's alive.

1025
01:14:57,070 --> 01:14:59,530
They don't come that way anymore.

1026
01:15:04,310 --> 01:15:05,670
Have l ever thought about it?

1027
01:15:08,020 --> 01:15:11,170
l've even been sucker enough to make plans.

1028
01:15:14,500 --> 01:15:19,120
You know, l saw an island in the Pacific once.

1029
01:15:19,120 --> 01:15:21,430
Never been able to forget it.

1030
01:15:24,980 --> 01:15:26,540
That's where l'd like to take her.

1031
01:15:28,820 --> 01:15:31,250
She'd have to be the sort of a girl...

1032
01:15:31,250 --> 01:15:34,900
...who'd jump in the surf with me and love it as much as l did.

1033
01:15:38,920 --> 01:15:46,210
You know, nights when you, the moon and the water all become one.

1034
01:15:47,280 --> 01:15:50,410
You feel you're part of something big and marvellous.

1035
01:15:52,990 --> 01:15:54,720
That's the only place to live.

1036
01:15:56,680 --> 01:15:58,860
The stars are so close overhead you feel

1037
01:15:58,860 --> 01:16:01,350
you could reach up and stir them around.

1038
01:16:07,530 --> 01:16:09,310
l've been thinking about it.

1039
01:16:11,200 --> 01:16:14,100
Boy, if l could ever find a girl who was hungry for those things.

1040
01:16:22,490 --> 01:16:24,990
Take me with you, Peter. Take me to your island.

1041
01:16:24,990 --> 01:16:27,940
l want to do all those things you talked about.

1042
01:16:29,160 --> 01:16:30,830
You better go back to your bed.

1043
01:16:32,370 --> 01:16:35,690
l love you. Nothing else matters. But we can run away.

1044
01:16:35,690 --> 01:16:39,670
Everything will take care of itself. Please, Peter...

1045
01:16:40,200 --> 01:16:42,870
...l can't let you out of my life now.

1046
01:16:44,010 --> 01:16:46,290
l couldn't live without you.

1047
01:16:56,410 --> 01:17:02,000
You'd better go back to your bed.

1048
01:17:12,000 --> 01:17:13,390
l'm sorry.

1049
01:17:49,180 --> 01:17:54,830
Hey, Brat! Did you mean that? Would you really go?

1050
01:18:35,340 --> 01:18:38,130
Look, all l'm asking is enough gas to get me to New York.

1051
01:18:38,190 --> 01:18:39,820
That bag's worth $25.

1052
01:18:40,300 --> 01:18:42,450
Yeah, but l got a bag. Wife gave me one for Christmas--

1053
01:18:42,450 --> 01:18:45,120
Hey listen, here's what l'll do. l'll come back in the morning...

1054
01:18:45,120 --> 01:18:47,540
...and buy it back from you with a $10 profit.

1055
01:18:47,540 --> 01:18:50,040
-What do you say?  -l ain't got a hat.

1056
01:18:50,040 --> 01:18:52,090
-What?  -l ain't got a hat.

1057
01:18:52,680 --> 01:18:55,170
Well, you got one now. Come on, fill her up.

1058
01:19:02,000 --> 01:19:06,580
Where you been all this time? Everybody's been asking about you.

1059
01:19:06,580 --> 01:19:07,600
Yeah, yeah, ok, get me one drink.

1060
01:19:07,600 --> 01:19:10,240
Nobody disturbs me for the next half hour.

1061
01:19:10,240 --> 01:19:11,710
Sure, boss.

1062
01:19:14,300 --> 01:19:15,240
Hello, Agnes.

1063
01:19:15,240 --> 01:19:18,670
-Don't. He'll shoot you on sight.  -Haven't been shot at in days.

1064
01:19:18,670 --> 01:19:22,310
-Get out of here! Get out! Get out!  -Now listen, Joe.

1065
01:19:22,310 --> 01:19:23,050
Don't "Joe" me.

1066
01:19:23,050 --> 01:19:24,360
All right, Joe. Listen.

1067
01:19:25,090 --> 01:19:26,320
You know l've always liked you.

1068
01:19:26,320 --> 01:19:28,660
Anytime l could help you, ran across a good story...

1069
01:19:28,660 --> 01:19:31,940
...l came running to you with it, didn't I? Well, l got one now.

1070
01:19:31,940 --> 01:19:34,480
The wires were on the level. The biggest scoop year.

1071
01:19:34,610 --> 01:19:36,430
-And I'm going to give it to you.  -You mean about the Andrews kid?

1072
01:19:36,430 --> 01:19:39,860
That's it! l've got it all written up, ready to go. All l want is a $1,000.

1073
01:19:39,860 --> 01:19:41,650
A $1,000? Get out of here before--

1074
01:19:41,650 --> 01:19:43,800
Don't get sore. You gotta do this for me.

1075
01:19:43,800 --> 01:19:46,420
l need a $1,000 and l need it quick. l'm in a jam.

1076
01:19:46,420 --> 01:19:47,900
What's the $1,000 for?

1077
01:19:47,900 --> 01:19:49,640
To tear down the walls of Jericho.

1078
01:19:49,640 --> 01:19:51,640
Never mind. Supposing if l told you that...

1079
01:19:51,640 --> 01:19:53,660
...Ellen Andrews will annul her marriage? No!

1080
01:19:53,660 --> 01:19:55,990
-Sh's going to marry somebody else.  -You're drunk.

1081
01:19:55,990 --> 01:19:57,930
Would such a story be worth $1,000 to you?

1082
01:19:57,930 --> 01:20:00,620
-lf it was on the level.  -l got it, Joe.

1083
01:20:03,190 --> 01:20:05,950
-Who's the guy she's gonna marry?  -l am, Joy.

1084
01:20:07,910 --> 01:20:09,440
-You?  -Yes.

1085
01:20:09,440 --> 01:20:12,890
Now l know you're drunk. l'm going home. Don't annoy me anymore.

1086
01:20:12,890 --> 01:20:14,990
For heaven sakes! Stop being an editor for a minute.

1087
01:20:15,930 --> 01:20:18,310
Listen, we know each other. You ought to know when l'm serious.

1088
01:20:18,310 --> 01:20:21,140
This is on the level. l met her on a bus from Miami.

1089
01:20:21,140 --> 01:20:23,570
l've been with her every minute. l'm in love with her, Joy.

1090
01:20:23,570 --> 01:20:26,540
You gotta get me this money now, quick. Minutes count.

1091
01:20:26,540 --> 01:20:28,950
She's waiting for me outside Philadelphia.

1092
01:20:28,950 --> 01:20:31,330
l gotta get right back. She doesn't even know l'm gone.

1093
01:20:32,210 --> 01:20:34,800
You know a guy can't propose to a gal without a cent in the world, can he?

1094
01:20:35,730 --> 01:20:40,130
What a story. On her way to join husband, Ellen Andrews--

1095
01:20:40,130 --> 01:20:41,320
That's it. That's it.

1096
01:20:43,350 --> 01:20:45,340
Let me see that a minute.

1097
01:20:47,880 --> 01:20:52,520
Zeke! Zeke! Zeke!

1098
01:20:52,520 --> 01:20:55,670
l told you, l told you, you couldn't trust him. He's gone.

1099
01:20:55,670 --> 01:20:56,410
Who?

1100
01:20:56,410 --> 01:20:58,130
The fella who was gonna stay a week. That's whom.

1101
01:20:58,130 --> 01:21:00,530
He skipped and took the car with him, too.

1102
01:21:00,530 --> 01:21:03,500
We wouldn't have known till morning if l hadn't took that magnesia.

1103
01:21:03,500 --> 01:21:07,090
Come on! Get up, don't lay there. Let's do something about it.

1104
01:21:07,560 --> 01:21:10,010
Well, there ain't nothing we can do if he's gone.

1105
01:21:24,110 --> 01:21:25,770
See that? They're gone.

1106
01:21:25,840 --> 01:21:29,290
Looks like it, don't it? What's this?

1107
01:21:30,060 --> 01:21:32,580
Ma! Here's the woman.

1108
01:21:32,650 --> 01:21:35,010
-What's the matter?  -Where's your husband, young lady?

1109
01:21:35,570 --> 01:21:38,470
-Husband?  -Yes, if he is your husband.

1110
01:21:40,880 --> 01:21:43,770
-lsn't he here?  -No, he ain't. The car's gone, too.

1111
01:21:45,920 --> 01:21:47,350
You got any money?

1112
01:21:48,260 --> 01:21:49,970
-No.  -Then you'll have to git!

1113
01:21:49,970 --> 01:21:51,970
Yeah. You'll have to git.

1114
01:21:54,820 --> 01:21:57,930
Please, may l use your phone? l've got to call New York.

1115
01:21:57,930 --> 01:21:59,450
You ain't gonna stick me for no phone call.

1116
01:21:59,450 --> 01:22:01,880
Go to the sheriff's office, a quarter mile down the road.

1117
01:22:01,880 --> 01:22:02,880
They'll fix you up.

1118
01:22:06,240 --> 01:22:08,430
And listen, next time you better not come back here.

1119
01:22:08,430 --> 01:22:10,620
l run a respectable place.

1120
01:22:14,460 --> 01:22:17,280
-Thanks, you saved my life.  -Okay. So long kid and good luck.

1121
01:22:17,280 --> 01:22:21,440
Thanks, goodbye. You're beautiful. All women are beautiful.

1122
01:22:22,150 --> 01:22:24,950
For my dough, he's still the best newspaper man in the business.

1123
01:22:25,510 --> 01:22:28,350
Get Hank, quick. Boy, what a yarn. what a yarn.

1124
01:22:28,380 --> 01:22:30,020
-Hello?  -Hold up the morning edition.

1125
01:22:30,020 --> 01:22:33,090
Break down the front page. We'll have a completely new layout.

1126
01:22:33,090 --> 01:22:36,570
Send in a couple of rewrite men. And Hank, listen. Don't do a thing.

1127
01:22:36,570 --> 01:22:39,280
l've got a story that'll make your hair curl. Wait a minute.

1128
01:22:39,280 --> 01:22:41,090
Yeah, yeah, don't annoy me, l'm busy.

1129
01:22:41,090 --> 01:22:43,300
Agnes, send Mike in here!

1130
01:22:43,300 --> 01:22:45,680
Dig up all the pictures on that Andrews kid.

1131
01:22:45,680 --> 01:22:48,300
And Hank, listen, get Haley out of bed.

1132
01:22:48,300 --> 01:22:50,320
l want a cartoon and l want it quick.

1133
01:22:50,930 --> 01:22:52,840
Westley's in it. He's waiting at the church...

1134
01:22:52,840 --> 01:22:56,030
...with tears on his face. The bride didn't show up.

1135
01:22:56,030 --> 01:22:57,910
Old Man Andrews is laughing his head off.

1136
01:22:57,910 --> 01:23:00,380
You know everything exaggerated. Yeah, snap into it.

1137
01:23:00,380 --> 01:23:01,440
Yeah, what is it?

1138
01:23:04,800 --> 01:23:06,950
Ellen Andrews? You're crazy.

1139
01:23:06,950 --> 01:23:07,970
No, l'm no crazy.

1140
01:23:07,970 --> 01:23:10,620
She phoned her father from an auto camp and coming here and get her.

1141
01:23:10,620 --> 01:23:13,530
He's getting a police escort and Westley's going along too.

1142
01:23:13,800 --> 01:23:16,520
Yeah, yeah, she's been travelling by bus.

1143
01:23:16,520 --> 01:23:18,250
The moment  she found out her father and Westley made up,

1144
01:23:18,250 --> 01:23:18,900
she phoned right in.

1145
01:23:19,470 --> 01:23:23,220
Okay, grab a car and stay with them. Get Hank again.

1146
01:23:23,220 --> 01:23:26,600
Agnes, get me a doctor, l'm gonna have a nervous breakdown.

1147
01:23:26,600 --> 01:23:28,800
Hank, forget what l told you. l'm having a nightmare, that's all.

1148
01:23:28,800 --> 01:23:32,690
Agnes, you call the police department. Tell them to find Peter Warne.

1149
01:23:32,690 --> 01:23:35,580
Send out a general alarm. l want that dirty crook pinched.

1150
01:23:35,580 --> 01:23:36,540
You want us?

1151
01:23:36,540 --> 01:23:38,100
Yeah, change the front page!

1152
01:23:38,100 --> 01:23:39,670
Ellen Andrews just phoned her father.

1153
01:23:39,670 --> 01:23:42,970
She's going home. The minute she found out Dad withdrew his objections.

1154
01:23:42,970 --> 01:23:45,510
She gave herself up. Spread it all over the place!

1155
01:23:45,510 --> 01:23:48,130
Play it up big! Major league! "Love Triumphant."

1156
01:23:48,130 --> 01:23:49,540
Go on, hop to it.

1157
01:23:49,540 --> 01:23:50,480
Okay.

1158
01:24:06,100 --> 01:24:09,310
Come on, baby. Come on! We gotta get there before she wakes up.

1159
01:24:20,590 --> 01:24:22,250
Can't you drive any faster?

1160
01:24:25,770 --> 01:24:32,670
"Young people in love are never hungry"

1161
01:24:41,050 --> 01:24:43,940
Come on, baby. We've got a police escort.

1162
01:24:55,150 --> 01:24:58,050
Come on, baby. They can't make a sucker out of us.

1163
01:25:01,600 --> 01:25:05,070
All right, come on. Step back. Give them room.

1164
01:25:05,070 --> 01:25:05,940
Come on, step back.

1165
01:25:09,470 --> 01:25:11,310
How about a picture for the paper, Mr. Andrews?

1166
01:25:11,310 --> 01:25:14,540
Wait till she gets home. Later, boys. Later.

1167
01:25:24,820 --> 01:25:28,750
"He floats through the air with the greatest of ease

1168
01:25:29,190 --> 01:25:33,010
"The daring young man on the flying trapeze"

1169
01:25:47,020 --> 01:25:48,510
Hey, get that thing out of the way!

1170
01:25:48,910 --> 01:25:51,140
Keep your britches on, we'll get it out.

1171
01:26:15,350 --> 01:26:16,610
Hey, you darn fool!

1172
01:27:22,810 --> 01:27:26,260
Hey, Pete! Ellen Andrews is going to marry that Westley guy again.

1173
01:27:35,640 --> 01:27:37,680
Gordon's out back some place.

1174
01:27:38,580 --> 01:27:41,580
When he comes in, give him this. Tell him l was just kidding.

1175
01:27:45,120 --> 01:27:47,690
-You can't get a thing done around here.  -Peter Warne was just in.

1176
01:27:47,690 --> 01:27:49,340
-What?  -He left this money.

1177
01:27:49,340 --> 01:27:51,120
-He said he was just kidding.  -Where is he?

1178
01:27:51,120 --> 01:27:52,940
-There he goes.  -Hey, Pete!

1179
01:27:57,750 --> 01:28:01,010
Hello, Joy. l'm sorry, it was just a little gag.

1180
01:28:01,010 --> 01:28:01,820
l thought l'd have some fun with you.

1181
01:28:01,820 --> 01:28:04,720
Yeah, sure you had me going for a little while, too.

1182
01:28:04,720 --> 01:28:07,840
-lt wouldn't have made a bad story at that.  -No, great.

1183
01:28:08,290 --> 01:28:11,710
But that's the way things go. You think you've got a great yarn...

1184
01:28:11,710 --> 01:28:16,820
...and then something comes along and messes up the finish. And there you are.

1185
01:28:16,820 --> 01:28:19,480
Yeah. Where am l?

1186
01:28:24,780 --> 01:28:27,470
When you sober up, come in and talk to me.

1187
01:28:29,410 --> 01:28:30,450
Thanks.

1188
01:28:55,260 --> 01:28:56,410
Ellie?

1189
01:28:57,020 --> 01:28:58,170
Oh, hello, Dad.

1190
01:28:58,370 --> 01:28:59,830
l knocked several times.

1191
01:29:00,800 --> 01:29:03,880
l'm sorry. l must have been daydreaming.

1192
01:29:03,880 --> 01:29:08,060
Well, everything's set. Creating quite a furore, too.

1193
01:29:08,630 --> 01:29:10,580
Great stunt King is going to pull.

1194
01:29:11,500 --> 01:29:12,360
Stunt?

1195
01:29:12,360 --> 01:29:14,980
Yeah, he's landing on the lawn in an autogyro.

1196
01:29:14,980 --> 01:29:19,610
Oh, oh, yes. Yes, l heard.

1197
01:29:19,610 --> 01:29:21,660
Personally, l think it's silly, too.

1198
01:29:22,930 --> 01:29:24,750
You look lovely, child.

1199
01:29:24,750 --> 01:29:26,690
Are you pleased with the gown?

1200
01:29:28,240 --> 01:29:29,010
Ellie?

1201
01:29:31,400 --> 01:29:34,520
Oh, the gown. Yes, it's nice, isn't it?

1202
01:29:40,810 --> 01:29:42,290
What's the matter, child?

1203
01:29:45,610 --> 01:29:46,740
What's wrong?

1204
01:29:46,740 --> 01:29:47,860
Nothing.

1205
01:29:48,880 --> 01:29:51,430
You haven't changed your mind about King, have you?

1206
01:29:51,430 --> 01:29:52,660
Oh, no.

1207
01:29:52,660 --> 01:29:57,230
Because if you have, it isn't too late. You know how l feel about him.

1208
01:29:57,230 --> 01:30:00,490
Well, you gave me such a scare when l couldn't find you.

1209
01:30:00,490 --> 01:30:03,420
You know, the old pump isn't what it used to be.

1210
01:30:03,970 --> 01:30:06,410
l'm sorry, Father.

1211
01:30:06,410 --> 01:30:08,030
l wouldn't hurt you for anything in the world. You know that.

1212
01:30:10,930 --> 01:30:11,360
What's the matter, child?

1213
01:30:12,510 --> 01:30:13,490
Aren't you happy?

1214
01:30:16,580 --> 01:30:17,890
l thought so.

1215
01:30:17,890 --> 01:30:24,800
l knew there was something on your mind.

1216
01:30:24,800 --> 01:30:29,100
There, now.

1217
01:30:29,100 --> 01:30:29,750
What's the matter?

1218
01:30:30,930 --> 01:30:33,930
You haven't fallen in love with someone else, have you?

1219
01:30:36,130 --> 01:30:37,610
Have you?

1220
01:30:40,970 --> 01:30:43,790
l haven't seen you cry since you were a baby.

1221
01:30:44,900 --> 01:30:46,840
This must be serious.

1222
01:30:48,380 --> 01:30:49,610
Where'd you meet him?

1223
01:30:51,930 --> 01:30:53,870
On the road.

1224
01:30:53,870 --> 01:30:56,780
Now don't tell me you've fallen in love with a bus driver?

1225
01:30:56,780 --> 01:31:02,890
Oh, no.

1226
01:31:02,890 --> 01:31:03,880
Who is he?

1227
01:31:05,270 --> 01:31:07,660
l don't know very much about him.

1228
01:31:07,980 --> 01:31:09,980
Except that l love him.

1229
01:31:10,990 --> 01:31:13,810
Well, if it's as serious as all that, we'll move heaven and earth to--

1230
01:31:13,810 --> 01:31:17,610
No, it's no use. He despises me.

1231
01:31:17,610 --> 01:31:18,990
Oh, Come now.

1232
01:31:18,990 --> 01:31:21,780
Yes, he does. He despises everything about me.

1233
01:31:22,400 --> 01:31:28,120
He says that l'm spoiled and selfish and pampered and thoroughly insincere.

1234
01:31:28,120 --> 01:31:30,330
Oh, ridiculous.

1235
01:31:30,330 --> 01:31:32,600
He doesn't think so much of you, either.

1236
01:31:33,270 --> 01:31:34,140
Well, l--

1237
01:31:34,140 --> 01:31:37,060
And he blames you for everything that's wrong with me.

1238
01:31:37,060 --> 01:31:39,880
He says you raised me stupidly.

1239
01:31:40,560 --> 01:31:43,040
And now that's a fine man to fall in love with.

1240
01:31:44,170 --> 01:31:45,580
He's marvellous.

1241
01:31:45,580 --> 01:31:49,150
Well, what are we going to do about it? Where is he?

1242
01:31:50,080 --> 01:31:52,850
-l don't know.  -l'd like to have a talk with him.

1243
01:31:52,850 --> 01:31:57,820
Oh, it wouldn't do any good. l practically threw myself at him.

1244
01:31:57,820 --> 01:32:01,680
Under the circumstances, don't you think we'd better call this thing off?.

1245
01:32:03,410 --> 01:32:04,940
No, l'll go through with it.

1246
01:32:04,940 --> 01:32:08,000
But that's silly. Seeing the way you feel about him.

1247
01:32:08,000 --> 01:32:11,340
No, it doesn't matter. l don't want to stir up any more trouble.

1248
01:32:11,340 --> 01:32:13,230
l've done it all my life.

1249
01:32:13,670 --> 01:32:17,440
l've made your life miserable. And mine, too.

1250
01:32:18,150 --> 01:32:24,310
l'm tired, father. l'm tired of running around in circles.

1251
01:32:24,310 --> 01:32:27,510
He's right, that's what l've been doing ever since l can remember.

1252
01:32:28,860 --> 01:32:30,510
l've got to settle down.

1253
01:32:31,470 --> 01:32:34,510
lt doesn't matter how, where, or with whom.

1254
01:32:36,360 --> 01:32:38,690
You've changed, Ellie.

1255
01:32:39,620 --> 01:32:43,880
l can't walk out on King now. lt would make us all look so ridiculous.

1256
01:32:45,310 --> 01:32:49,070
Anyway, what difference does it make?

1257
01:32:49,750 --> 01:32:51,630
l'll never see Peter again.

1258
01:32:51,940 --> 01:32:53,370
ls that his name?

1259
01:32:55,500 --> 01:32:56,910
Peter Warne.

1260
01:32:58,410 --> 01:33:00,510
Peter Warne.

1261
01:33:02,910 --> 01:33:04,390
Why, do you know him?

1262
01:33:04,390 --> 01:33:06,170
Why, no, no.

1263
01:33:06,170 --> 01:33:08,910
Oh, father, you haven't heard from him, have you?

1264
01:33:08,910 --> 01:33:12,100
-Don't be silly, of course.  -Please, what's that?

1265
01:33:25,930 --> 01:33:28,780
Well, l guess that was his only interest in me, wasn't it?

1266
01:33:28,780 --> 01:33:32,150
-The reward.  -l'm sorry you read it.

1267
01:33:32,150 --> 01:33:35,270
-Are you going to see him?  -l suppose so.

1268
01:33:35,270 --> 01:33:40,460
Certainly. Pay him off. He's entitled to it. He did an excellent job.

1269
01:33:40,460 --> 01:33:45,150
He kept me thoroughly entertained. lt's worth every penny he gets.

1270
01:33:45,150 --> 01:33:47,930
Oh, thank you, Mary. That's just what l needed.

1271
01:33:47,930 --> 01:33:49,940
Mr. Westley's on his way up.

1272
01:33:50,050 --> 01:33:51,710
Fine, have him come in.

1273
01:33:59,020 --> 01:34:00,310
l'll be going.

1274
01:34:12,000 --> 01:34:15,010
well, if it isn't the bridegroom himself. You're just in time, King.

1275
01:34:15,010 --> 01:34:16,860
How are you, Ellie?

1276
01:34:16,860 --> 01:34:18,100
You happy?

1277
01:34:18,170 --> 01:34:20,860
Happy? Why shouldn't l be happy?

1278
01:34:20,930 --> 01:34:23,010
Here we are, let's drink.

1279
01:34:23,550 --> 01:34:27,130
lt's up to you now. l want our life to be full of excitement.

1280
01:34:27,130 --> 01:34:30,100
We'll never let up, will we? Never a dull moment.

1281
01:34:30,100 --> 01:34:32,880
We'll get on a merry-go-round and never get off.

1282
01:34:33,500 --> 01:34:35,830
Promise you'll never let me get off.

1283
01:34:35,830 --> 01:34:38,000
Whatever you say, darling. lt's a promise.

1284
01:34:52,400 --> 01:34:56,630
Hello? Yeah. Who?

1285
01:34:59,490 --> 01:35:00,830
Why can't l see you at your office?

1286
01:35:01,180 --> 01:35:04,440
l'm leaving for Washington tonight. l may be gone several weeks.

1287
01:35:04,510 --> 01:35:07,510
l thought, perhaps, you'd like to get this thing settled.

1288
01:35:08,510 --> 01:35:10,840
Yeah. But l don't like the idea of butting in on your jamboree.

1289
01:35:11,230 --> 01:35:14,390
Between you and me, those things give me a stiff pain.

1290
01:35:14,390 --> 01:35:17,790
You don't have to see anybody. You can come directly to my study.

1291
01:35:17,790 --> 01:35:20,150
No. Why do l wanna--

1292
01:35:23,390 --> 01:35:28,010
Hey, wait a minute, wait a minute. Maybe l will come over. Yeah.

1293
01:35:28,010 --> 01:35:31,050
l'd like to get a load of that three ring circus you're pulling.

1294
01:35:31,050 --> 01:35:34,060
Yeah, l wanna see what love looks like when it's triumphant.

1295
01:35:34,430 --> 01:35:35,960
l haven't had a good laugh in a week.

1296
01:35:38,880 --> 01:35:40,060
Mr. Warne?

1297
01:35:40,170 --> 01:35:40,860
Yeah.

1298
01:35:44,290 --> 01:35:46,180
-Sit down.  -Thanks.

1299
01:35:46,990 --> 01:35:51,250
l was surprised to get your note. My daughter hadn't told me anything...

1300
01:35:51,250 --> 01:35:52,860
...about you. About your helping her.

1301
01:35:52,860 --> 01:35:55,620
That's typical of your daughter. Takes those things for granted.

1302
01:35:56,040 --> 01:35:58,360
Why did she think l lugged her from Miami, for the  fivert?

1303
01:35:58,750 --> 01:36:01,610
She thinks you're entitled to anything you can get.

1304
01:36:01,610 --> 01:36:05,860
Oh, she does? lsn't that sweet of her? You don't, l suppose.

1305
01:36:05,860 --> 01:36:10,420
Well, l don't know. l'll have to see on what you base your claim.

1306
01:36:10,420 --> 01:36:12,260
l presume you feel justified.

1307
01:36:12,260 --> 01:36:15,720
lf l didn't, l wouldn't be here. l got it all itemised.

1308
01:36:18,820 --> 01:36:23,450
"Cash outlay, $8.60. Top coat, $15.

1309
01:36:23,450 --> 01:36:26,350
"Suitcase, $7.50. Hat, $4.

1310
01:36:26,350 --> 01:36:32,540
"Three shirts, $4.50. Total, $39.60.

1311
01:36:32,540 --> 01:36:36,120
"All of the above items had to be sold to buy gasoline."

1312
01:36:36,120 --> 01:36:39,090
And l sold some shorts and socks, too. l'm throwing those in.

1313
01:36:39,090 --> 01:36:42,020
-Yes, l know.  -What's the matter? lsn't it cheap enough?

1314
01:36:42,830 --> 01:36:45,320
Trip like that'd cost you a $1,000, maybe more.

1315
01:36:45,320 --> 01:36:46,940
Now, let me get this straight.

1316
01:36:46,940 --> 01:36:51,100
You want $39.60 in addition to the $10,000?

1317
01:36:51,100 --> 01:36:52,380
What 10,000?

1318
01:36:53,170 --> 01:36:54,510
The reward.

1319
01:36:55,580 --> 01:36:57,430
Who said anything about a reward?

1320
01:36:57,850 --> 01:37:00,500
l'm afraid l'm a little bit confused. l assumed--

1321
01:37:00,500 --> 01:37:03,350
Look, look, look, all l want is $39.60.

1322
01:37:03,350 --> 01:37:05,330
lf you give me a check for it, l'll get out of this joint.

1323
01:37:05,330 --> 01:37:06,920
lt gives me the jitters.

1324
01:37:07,970 --> 01:37:11,170
-You're a peculiar chap.  -We'll go into that some other time.

1325
01:37:11,170 --> 01:37:13,360
The average man would go after the reward.

1326
01:37:13,360 --> 01:37:15,820
Did anybody ever make a sucker out of you?

1327
01:37:16,490 --> 01:37:19,940
lt's a matter of principle. You probably wouldn't understand.

1328
01:37:19,940 --> 01:37:21,830
When anybody takes me for a buggy ride,

1329
01:37:21,830 --> 01:37:23,570
l don't like paying for the privilege.

1330
01:37:23,570 --> 01:37:25,580
Were you taken for a buggy ride?

1331
01:37:25,580 --> 01:37:29,730
Yes. With all the trimmings. So how about the check, do l get it?

1332
01:37:30,190 --> 01:37:31,770
-Certainly.  -Thanks.

1333
01:37:46,840 --> 01:37:48,220
Here you are.

1334
01:37:48,220 --> 01:37:49,260
Thank you.

1335
01:37:50,960 --> 01:37:54,450
Wait, do you mind if l ask you a question, frankly?

1336
01:37:54,450 --> 01:37:56,340
Do you love my daughter?

1337
01:37:57,910 --> 01:38:00,960
Any guy in love with your daughter should be examined.

1338
01:38:00,960 --> 01:38:02,230
No, that's an evasion.

1339
01:38:02,230 --> 01:38:04,810
She picked herself a perfect running mate,

1340
01:38:04,810 --> 01:38:06,800
King Westley. The pill of the century.

1341
01:38:06,800 --> 01:38:09,520
She needs a guy that'd sock her once a day

1342
01:38:09,520 --> 01:38:10,970
whether it's coming to her or not.

1343
01:38:10,970 --> 01:38:14,270
lf you were wiser, you'd have done it yourself long ago.

1344
01:38:14,270 --> 01:38:15,240
Do you love her?

1345
01:38:15,240 --> 01:38:18,260
A normal man couldn't live with her without going nutty.

1346
01:38:18,260 --> 01:38:19,870
She's my idea of nothing.

1347
01:38:19,870 --> 01:38:22,240
l asked you a simple question! Do you love her?

1348
01:38:22,240 --> 01:38:26,400
Yes! Now don't hold that against me! l'm a little screwy myself!

1349
01:38:29,080 --> 01:38:32,280
Well, here's to the merry-go-round.

1350
01:38:38,040 --> 01:38:40,410
Perfect. Now you look natural.

1351
01:38:46,230 --> 01:38:48,490
-l hope you got your money.  -You bet l did.

1352
01:38:48,490 --> 01:38:51,180
-Congratulations.  -Thanks. Same to you.

1353
01:38:51,940 --> 01:38:54,850
Stay around and watch the fun. You'll enjoy it immensely.

1354
01:38:54,850 --> 01:38:56,890
l would, but l've got a weak stomach.

1355
01:39:03,840 --> 01:39:06,540
-l just had a long talk with him.  -l'm not interested.

1356
01:39:06,890 --> 01:39:07,950
Now just a minute, Ellie.

1357
01:39:07,950 --> 01:39:10,340
l don't want to hear another word about him.

1358
01:39:23,560 --> 01:39:26,740
Come on, folks. King Westley has arrived. Come on!

1359
01:40:20,420 --> 01:40:22,110
Here they come, boys. Turn them over.

1360
01:40:51,250 --> 01:40:53,090
You're a sucker to go through with this.

1361
01:40:55,020 --> 01:40:56,630
That guy, Warne, is okay.

1362
01:40:57,290 --> 01:41:02,150
He didn't want the reward. All he asked for was $39.60.

1363
01:41:02,150 --> 01:41:05,120
lt's what he spent on you. Said it was a matter of principle.

1364
01:41:05,120 --> 01:41:06,740
You took him for a ride.

1365
01:41:13,770 --> 01:41:18,320
He loves you, Ellie. He told me so.

1366
01:41:19,990 --> 01:41:22,340
You don't want to be married to a mug like Westley.

1367
01:41:23,470 --> 01:41:25,430
l can buy him off for a pot of gold.

1368
01:41:29,710 --> 01:41:31,990
And you can make an old man happy.

1369
01:41:32,230 --> 01:41:34,350
And you won't do so bad for yourself.

1370
01:41:35,430 --> 01:41:38,670
lf you change your mind, your car's waiting at the back gate.

1371
01:41:49,840 --> 01:41:52,960
Dearly beloved, we are gathered together here in the sight of God...

1372
01:41:52,960 --> 01:41:55,220
...and in the face of this company,

1373
01:41:55,220 --> 01:41:56,910
to join together this man and this woman...

1374
01:41:56,910 --> 01:41:58,570
...in holy matrimony. lf any man can show

1375
01:41:58,570 --> 01:42:01,330
just cause why they may not lawfully...

1376
01:42:01,330 --> 01:42:04,490
...be joined together, let him now speak or else,

1377
01:42:04,490 --> 01:42:07,660
hereafter forever, hold his peace.

1378
01:42:09,660 --> 01:42:13,150
King, will thou have this woman to thy wedded wife

1379
01:42:13,150 --> 01:42:14,490
so long as you both shall live?

1380
01:42:14,840 --> 01:42:15,850
l will.

1381
01:42:17,090 --> 01:42:20,560
Ellen, will thou have this man to thy wedded husband...

1382
01:42:20,560 --> 01:42:23,040
..so long as you both shall live?

1383
01:42:26,930 --> 01:42:27,990
Ellen!

1384
01:42:28,570 --> 01:42:29,560
Ellie!

1385
01:43:00,770 --> 01:43:01,780
What happened?

1386
01:43:01,780 --> 01:43:03,800
l haven't the slightest idea.

1387
01:43:19,100 --> 01:43:23,040
Don't want to talk to you. Don't want to talk to anybody.

1388
01:43:23,040 --> 01:43:24,660
Don't want to see anybody.

1389
01:43:24,660 --> 01:43:26,550
But it's King Westley on the phone.

1390
01:43:30,090 --> 01:43:33,250
Hello, my would be ex-son-in-law.

1391
01:43:33,250 --> 01:43:36,900
l've sent you a check for $100,000.

1392
01:43:36,900 --> 01:43:38,510
That's the smartest thing you ever did, Westley,

1393
01:43:38,510 --> 01:43:41,280
not to contest that annulment.

1394
01:43:41,730 --> 01:43:45,650
That's satisfactory, isn't it? lt ought to be.

1395
01:43:45,650 --> 01:43:50,210
l'm not complaining. Not complaining. lt was dirt-cheap.

1396
01:43:50,940 --> 01:43:53,140
Don't fall out of any windows!

1397
01:43:54,720 --> 01:43:57,830
There's another wire from Peter. They're in Glen Falls, Michigan.

1398
01:43:58,540 --> 01:44:02,480
"What's holding up the annulment, you slowpoke.

1399
01:44:02,480 --> 01:44:05,500
"The walls of Jericho are toppling."

1400
01:44:07,140 --> 01:44:12,350
Send him a telegram right away. Just say, "Let them topple."

1401
01:44:14,900 --> 01:44:16,940
-Funny couple, ain't they?  -Yeah.

1402
01:44:16,940 --> 01:44:19,300
lf you ask me, l don't believe they're married.

1403
01:44:19,300 --> 01:44:21,730
They're married, all right. l just seen the license.

1404
01:44:22,580 --> 01:44:23,730
They made me get them a rope and a blanket,

1405
01:44:23,730 --> 01:44:26,170
on a night like this.

1406
01:44:26,170 --> 01:44:27,760
What do you reckon that's for?

1407
01:44:27,760 --> 01:44:30,480
Blamed if l know. l just brought them a trumpet.

1408
01:44:30,480 --> 01:44:31,450
A trumpet?

1409
01:44:32,060 --> 01:44:33,960
A toy. They sent me to the store to get it.

1410
01:44:33,960 --> 01:44:36,390
What in the world do they want a trumpet for?

1411
01:44:36,390 --> 01:44:37,770
Don't know.

